\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Recent economic comments from China's top officials\b0\par\par\uc2 433 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2012\par 09:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BEIJING, Sept 10 (Reuters) - China's leaders have pledged to step up policy fine-tuning in the second-half of 2012 to bolster an economy that slowed to its weakest pace of growth in more than three years in the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to cut interest rates and bank reserve requirement ratios in coming months to support growth.\par \par \uc2 Below are recent comments on the economy from members of the top government leadership and senior institutional chiefs.\par \par \uc2 XIN CHANGXING, VICE MINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCES AND SOCIAL SECURITY\par \par \uc2 "Based on our surveys on 600 companies, they are keeping the level of employment stable. The total amount of workers employed is almost in line with last year. China has not seen any widespread layoffs.\par \par \uc2 "But the slowing economic growth is starting to affect the employment situation gradually, with the growth pace of newly created jobs moderating since April."\par \par \uc2 "Based on our survey of more than 100 job markets, demand for workers and the number of job hunters are both decelerating."\par \par \uc2 SOURCE: News conference, Sep 10\par \par \uc2 ZHONG SHAN, VICE COMMERCE MINISTER\par \par \uc2 "China's trade situation is very grim this year and it is very difficult to achieve the growth target set earlier this year."\par \par \uc2 SOURCE: International Business Daily, Aug 29\par \par \uc2 WANG CHAO, VICE COMMERCE MINISTER\par \par \uc2 "China and the United States should improve macro-economic policy coordination, work together to fight trade protectionism and avoid politicising trade issues.\par \par \uc2 "The two countries should also broaden the scope of trade and investment with each other.\par \par \uc2 "China has been focusing on boosting domestic consumption and transforming its economic growth model, which will create more investment opportunities for foreign countries, including the United States."\par \par \uc2 SOURCE: An academic forum in Beijing, Aug 28\par \par \uc2 YI GANG, HEAD OF CHINA'S STATE ADMINISTRATION OF \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 "The exchange rate of the renminbi is very close to equilibrium. With China's GDP per capita exceeding 5,000 yuan ($795), domestic companies will grow rapidly, which may continue for 20 years.\par \par \uc2 "China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stayed steady over the past year, showing that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees basically balanced cross-border capital inflows and outflows."\par \par \uc2 SOURCE: China Securities Journal, July 23\par \par \uc2 LI KEQIANG, VICE PREMIER\par \par \uc2 "China should stick to the general principle of seeking growth while maintaining stability and strive to expand domestic\par \par \uc2 consumption in order to stabilize economic growth."\par \par \uc2 SOURCE: \uc2 Xinhua\uc2 , July 14\par \par \uc2 (Reporting By China Economics Team)\par \par \uc2 CHINA-ECONOMY/OFFICIALS (FACTBOX) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | O | OIL | Z | ABX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120910e89a000d0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
