\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Majors\b0\par\par\uc2 1,875 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2012\par 01:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range   Larger Range \par USD/JPY    78.18-78.65      78.07-78.84 \par EUR/USD   1.2546-1.2637    1.2487-1.2693 \par AUD/USD   1.0272-1.0354    1.0203-1.0398 \par NZD/USD   0.7965-0.8042    0.7932-0.8057 \par GBP/USD   1.5769-1.5895    1.5751-1.5911 \par USD/CHF   0.9500-0.9569    0.9475-0.9617 \par USD/CAD   0.9838-0.9931    0.9825-0.9948 \par EUR/JPY    97.98-99.04      97.87-99.18 \par EUR/GBP   0.7899-0.7963    0.7887-0.8000 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent high and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/JPY - to trade with risks skewed lower. Liquidity likely thin later in global day as U.S. markets are shut today for Labor Day holiday. USD/JPY undermined by weaker USD sentiment on prospect of further U.S. quantitative easing after Federal Reserve Chairman Bernanke expressed dissatisfaction with the economic outlook and repeated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "will provide additional policy accommodation as needed" to support the economic recovery. USD/JPY also weighed by lower \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields; Japan exporter sales; flows to safe-haven JPY and unwinding of JPY-funded carry trades amid increased risk aversion as China's official PMI fell to nine-month low of 49.2 in August (vs 50.0 forecast), heightening concerns about global economic slowdown. But USD/JPY losses tempered by demand from Japan importers. USD