ent. Daily chart mixed as MACD in bullish mode, but stochastics neutral. Support at 0.9848-0.9838 band (Friday's low-Aug. 21 three-month low); breach would turn near-term outlook negative, targeting 0.9825 (May 3 low), then 0.9796 (April 27 low), 0.9776 (Sept. 16, 2011 low) and 0.9721 (Aug. 31, 2011 low). Resistance at 0.9931 (Thursday's high), then at 0.9948 (Aug. 23 high) and 0.9969 (Aug. 10 high); breach would target 0.9988 (Aug. 8 high), then 1.0012-1.0022 band (Aug. 7 high-Aug. 6 high), 1.0078-1.0085 band (Aug. 3 high-Aug. 2 high) and 1.0105 (July 27 high).\par \par \uc2 EUR/JPY - to trade with risks skewed lower. Undermined by weaker investor risk appetite after disappointing China official PMI data; Japan exporter sales. But EUR/JPY downside limited by demand from Japan importers; hopes that the ECB would reveal a bond-buying plan to combat the euro-zone sovereign debt crisis at Thursday's policy meeting. Daily chart mixed as MACD bullish, but stochastics bearish at overbought; five-day moving average meandering sideways. Support at 97.98 (Friday's low), then at 97.87 (Tuesday's low) and 97.72 (Aug. 17 low); breach would expose downside to 96.99 (Aug. 16 low), then 96.53 (Aug. 15 low), 95.95 (Aug. 13 low) and 95.72 (Aug. 10 low). Resistance at 99.03-99.04 (Friday's high-Aug. 22 high), then at 99.18 (Aug. 21 high); breach would expose upside to 99.80 (100-day moving average), then psychological 100.00 line and 100.84 (July 3 high).\par \par \uc2 EUR/GBP - to trade in lower range. Daily chart mixed as MACD bullish, but stochastics bearish overbought; five-day moving average meandering sideways. Support at 0.7899 (Thursday's low), then at 0.7887 (Aug. 24 low) and 0.7874 (Aug. 22 low); breach would target 0.7852 (Aug. 21 low), then 0.7831 (Aug. 20 low), 0.7810 (Aug. 16 reaction low) and 0.7787 (July 30 low). Resistance at 0.7958-0.7963 band (Friday's high-Aug. 6 high); breach would expose upside to 0.8000 (61.8% Fibonacci retracement of 0.8153-0.7753 June 11-July