\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW: \uc2 PBOC\uc2  Shifting Tactic on Yuan Guidance, Allowing Market Bigger Role - UFJ Analyst\b0\par\par\uc2 661 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2012\par 06:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ analyst says yuan fixing more in line with market levels in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 -- He says \uc2 PBOC\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on daily basis when yuan selling was heavy.\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI--\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has set the yuan's reference exchange rate more in line with market levels in recent weeks, taking a small but important step toward fulfilling its long-standing pledge to let market forces play a bigger role in determining the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value, Cliff Tan, East Asian Head of Global Markets Research with \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ, told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 "I can definitely say today, there is no doubt in my mind, that the Chinese authorities are allowing the market to set the exchange rate much more than they were four months ago," Mr. Tan said.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  in mid-April doubled the yuan's trading band against the dollar to 1.0% above and below the central parity, its daily reference exchange rate, from 0.5% previously.\par \par \uc2 The decision to liberalize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime a bit more came as Beijing started unveiling a series of reforms aimed at improving China's rigid and inefficient financial system by allowing banks more freedom to set interest rates and granting private capital more access to sectors traditionally dominated by the state.\par \par \uc2 However, the yuan traded in a very narrow range against the dollar in the first three or four weeks following the band widening as the authorities continued to keep a firm grip on the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mr. Tan said.\par \par \uc2 The spot yuan moved very closely around the fixing during that period, usually weakened by no more than 0.5% from the central parity, the original band.\par \par \uc2 "Then people started to get nervous about Europe again, and there was a kind of general risk-off sentiment returning to the market, and... 'capital seepage' out of China probably picked up into the May, June, July months," he said, referring to signs of capital outflows from China around that time.\par \par \uc2 During that period, the yuan suffered waves of heavy selling, often weakening substantially from the fixing, before finally hitting its daily downside limit in late July.\par \par \uc2 The strong selling pressure on the yuan and the market's volatility at that time forced the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on a daily basis, Mr. Tan said.\par \par \uc2 "They kept trying for many weeks... to see if the fixing could influence where the spot was trading, but the spot kept deviating further and further away. Once you got close to the 1% range, they would have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 However, the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  appears to have changed its tactic and mindset in recent trading sessions, aligning the yuan's fixing more closely to market levels, which has helped reduce the necessity of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gives the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more policy flexibility in general, Mr. Tan said.\par \par \uc2 Citing his own observations, Mr. Tan said the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  had initially set the fixing at an average of around 500 pips away from the yuan's spot trading level soon after the band widening, before letting it narrow to around 300 pips in recent sessions.\par \par \uc2 Despite the encouraging shift by the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 , there is a long way to go before the market eventually has bigger say in determining the yuan's value.\par \par \uc2 "Just for illustration purposes, my judgment would be that the market is only playing a 10% role in determining where dollar-China [yuan] really trades," said Mr. Tan.\par \par \uc2 But he expects the percentage to increase over the next two to three years, as he believes the authorities will continue to loosen their grip on the exchange rate and allow the market to play a bigger role.\par \par \uc2 --Shen Hong contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Wynne Wang at wynne.wang@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2  [ 08-08-12 0447GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120808e88800081\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
