\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Recent economic comments from China's top officials\b0\par\par\uc2 1,204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2012\par 03:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  BEIJING, July 23 (Reuters) - China's growth rate slowed for a sixth successive quarter in the second three months of 2012 to 7.6 percent, its slackest pace in more than three years, highlighting the need for more policy vigilance from Beijing even as signs emerge that action taken so far, is beginning to stabilise the economy.\par \par \uc2  Below are recent comments on the economy from members of the top government leadership and senior institutional chiefs.\par \par \uc2  YI GANG, HEAD OF CHINA'S STATE ADMINISTRATION OF \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  "The exchange rate of the renminbi is very close to an equilibrium level. With China's GDP per capita exceeding 5,000 yuan ($794), outbound investment by domestic companies will grow rapidly, which may continue for 20 years.\par \par \uc2  "China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stayed at a steady level over the past year, showing that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees basically balanced cross-border capital inflows and outflows." \par \par \uc2  Source: China Securities Journal, July 23\par \par \uc2  LI KEQIANG, VICE PREMIER\par \par \uc2  "China should stick to the general principle of seeking growth while maintaining stability and strive to expand domestic consumption in order to stabilize economic growth."\par \par \uc2  Source: Xinhua, July 14\par \par \uc2  WEN JIABAO, PREMIER \par \par \uc2  "The measures to stabilise economic growth include boosting consumption and diversifying exports, but currently, what is important is to pursue a reasonable growth of investment.\par \par \uc2  "Stabilising economic growth is not just an urgent task at the moment, but also an arduous task over the long term."\par \par \uc2  Source: Government website, July 10\par \par \uc2  WEN JIABAO, PREMIER\par \par \uc2  "China's current economic situation is generally stable, but it still faces relatively huge downward pressure. We should increase the strength of policy fine-tuning.\par \par \uc2  "China should maintain its proactive fiscal policy, focusing particularly on improving the structural tax cut policies, while continuing to implement prudent monetary policy to effectively settle the structural contradiction between the supply and demand of credit."\par \par \uc2  Source: Xinhua, July 8\par \par \uc2  WEN JIABAO, PREMIER\par \par \uc2  "Currently, the property market adjustment is still at a crucial stage and we must unswervingly continue the work and make the fight against speculative property investment demand a long-term policy.\par \par \uc2  "We must not allow housing prices to rebound that will waste all of our previous efforts."\par \par \uc2  Source: Xinhua, July 7\par \par \uc2  ZHANG XIAOQIANG, VICE CHAIRMAN, NATIONAL DEVELOPMENT AND REFORM COMMISSION\par \par \uc2  "The country's policy is to gradually open up its capital account and realise the full convertibility of the yuan.\par \par \uc2  "Qianhai, as the first experimental zone of the country's modern service industry, should be a pioneer of that."\par \par \uc2  Source: News conference, June 29\par \par \uc2  CHEN DEMING, COMMERCE MINISTER\par \par \uc2  "The trade situation is still relatively grim afterwards, and if lucky, we will be able to keep annual growth of around 10 percent."\par \par \uc2  Source: Xinhua news agency, June 11\par \par \uc2  LI KEQIANG, VICE PREMIER  \par \par \uc2  "We must stick to the long-term strategy of stimulating  domestic demand in order to maintain stable and relatively fast  economic growth. It is also an important step to reform our  economic structure."  \par \par \uc2  Source: State radio, May 30  \par \par \uc2  LI JINZAO, VICE MINISTER OF COMMERCE    \par \par \uc2  "There are signs of things turning better from data in the  first 10 days of May. They are making us more confident about  achieving this year's trade target.  \par \par \uc2  "But we also clearly know that there will be no quick and  significant improvement in the global situation, and we are  still confronted with a relatively stern trade environment."  \par \par \uc2  Source: News conference, May 25  \par \par \uc2  ZHOU XIAOCHUAN, \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  GOVERNOR    \par \par \uc2  "The financial reform in Wenzhou will be a process of  constant exploration, which needs relevant state departments and the governments of Zhejiang province, as well as Wenzhou city,  to think about how to serve the real economy and solve acute  financial problems in Wenzhou.   \par \par \uc2  "We need to further liberalise our thoughts, become more  confident, cut restrictions, encourage private investors,  support innovation and explore bravely to push ahead the reform  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in an active, steady and smooth manner."    \par  Source: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  statement, May 25    \par     \par  WEN JIABAO, PREMIER    \par  "China's domestic economy is still facing some protruding \par problems and particularly the downward economic pressure is \par increasing.    \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "We should put economic growth at a more important position \par and increase the strength of policy fine-tuning to make it more \par targeted, flexible and forward-looking.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "As for projects that have got government approval, such as \par in the fields of railway, energy-saving, rural and western \par regional infrastructure, education and healthcare, we should \par speed up the pace of construction."    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Source: State Council meeting, May 23        \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  ZHANG PING, NATIONAL DEVELOPMENT AND REFORM COMMISSION CHIEF\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "First of all, we need to maintain steady and relatively \par fast economic growth - development is the key for resolving all \par problems in China.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "It's a dilemma to stabilise growth and stabilise inflation.\par Even though inflation has showed signs of stabilisation, we \par cannot lower our guard against price rises.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "Currently, the situation concerning prices is still severe \par -- global liquidity is ample and global commodity prices are \par fluctuating at high levels. Pressures on prices will stay over \par the long term."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Source: Speech, May 18  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  CHEN DEMING, MINISTER OF COMMERCE    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "In the medium to long term, the yuan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  formation \par mechanism needs further improvement.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "First, for the yuan to become convertible under the capital\par account, apart from the current account, China must establish a \par firewall to keep out global financial risks. Therefore, the \par opening-up must be gradual.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "Overall, the Chinese yuan still has a long way to go to \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par become a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for global settlement."    \par  Source: Interview with Caixin magazine, April 9    \par  LI KEQIANG, VICE PREMIER    \par  "Expanding domestic consumption is our top priority in \par adjusting the economic structure."    \par  Source: Speech at Boao Forum, April 2    \par  WEN JIABAO, PREMIER   \par  "As for yuan internationalisation, when it is coming, you \par can't stop it even if you want to stop it ... but when the \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 timing is not right, then an early implementation of it is not \par possible.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "Foreign friends must firmly believe in this. China's policy\par direction can't change and won't change ... China's economic and\par trade relations with the rest of the world can only be enhanced,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not be weakened."    \par  Source: Speech at China Development Forum, March 19    \par  LI KEQIANG, VICE PREMIER    \par  "China has reached a crucial period in changing its economic\par model and (change) cannot be delayed. Reforms have entered a \par tough stage."    \par  Source: Speech at China Development Forum, March 18    \par  \par  WEN JIABAO, PREMIER    \par  "Reform has reached a critical stage. Without the success of\par political reform, economic reforms cannot be carried out. The \par results that we have achieved may be lost.    \par  "Economic development has also produced unfair distribution,\par a lack of trust, graft and other problems.    \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "I'm deeply aware that solving these problems needs the \par advance of political system reform, as well as economic system \par reform, and especially reform of the leadership system of the \par party and state."    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Source: National People's Congress news conference, March 14\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by China Economics Tea [20120723 015747 GMT] \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 m; Editing by Nick Edwards) [20120723 015747 GMT] \f28 \par \par \uc2 CHINA-ECONOMY/OFFICIALS (FACTBOX) | ABN | C | GRO | MTL | SOF | D | E | RBN | M | O | OIL | Z|CHINA-ECONOMY/OFFICIALS (FACTBOX)=2 | ABN | C | GRO | MTL | SOF | D | E | RBN | M | O | OIL | Z|chained   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120726e87n0002s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
