\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan opens firmer, c.bank sets higher midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2012\par 08:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * C.bank raises midpoint on weaker dollar\par \par \uc2 * Spot prices stay flat, traders await new developments\par \par \uc2 * Traders see floor at 6.38 per dollar on c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Pete Sweeney\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, July 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set a higher midpoint for the yuan for the fifth consecutive day as the dollar moved away from a two-year high against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though the spot market remained anemic.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 set the official midpoint\par \par \uc2 at 6.3112 per dollar on Friday morning, continuing to firm the yuan against the greenback as the dollar index kept up its gradual slide away from a peak hit July 12.\par \par \uc2 Traders said they saw no strong signals from the U.S. that it is prepared to ease monetary policy again to spur growth -- which would put negative pressure on the dollar's exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Large clients are also cautious, and dollar buying sentiment has ebbed over the course of the week, resulting in an extremely narrow range for spot prices, traders said. Spot yuan has traded in a range between 6.3792 and 6.3681 -- only 111 points apart -- but the yuan has not moved over 54 points on any single day. It was trading at 6.3732 early in the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 "There hasn't been any big change this week," said a trader at a foreign bank in Shanghai. "The U.S. Fed and Bernanke did not say anything new. The yuan is trading slightly above 6.38; it looks like there's a degree of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 6.38."\par \par \uc2 Traders say that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is using strong midpoints to signal to the market that it will not allow the yuan to weaken past 6.4 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 OFFSHORE MARKETS\par \par \uc2 The yuan also had a quiet week offshore. The one-year non-deliverable forward strengthened slightly this week but continued to trade at a discount to the spot price at 6.4130.\par \par \uc2 Offshore yuan traded in Hong Kong CNH remained close to the onshore price at 6.3720.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Pete Sweeney; Editing by Joseph Radford)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN-MIDDAY | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120723e87k0009a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
