\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 548 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 2012\par 03:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: GROWTH PACT HELD UP AS ITALY, SPAIN CALL FOR IMMEDIATE HELP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Talks at a European Union summit appeared deadlocked early Friday with Italy, Spain and the U.K. refusing to sign off on a 120 billion euro growth pact. (published 0025 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN OUTPUT, PRICE DATA SUGGEST RECOVERY YET TO TAKE HOLD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese industrial production fell a worse-than-expected 3.1% in May from the previous month while consumer prices were lower in the period, the government said Friday, in a sign that a recovery in the domestic economy has yet to take hold. (published 0041 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: SOUTH KOREA INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 1.1% ON MONTH; BEATS FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's industrial production increaed at a faster pace in May than in the preceding month, beating forecasts, government data showed Thursday. (published 2303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HOLLANDE:FRANCE WANTS DEEPER EUROPEAN INTEGRATION ONLY WITHIN EURO ZONE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 France is ready to allow for power transfer to European Union institutions only if the process is limited to the 17 euro-zone countries, French President Francois Hollande said Thursday, as he called for a quick implementation of a budgetary and banking union within the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  zone. (published 0042 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par U.K., FRANCE, GERMANY FAIL TO AGREE ON EU PATENT COURT HQ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K., France and Germany failed to agree on the location of a new European Union patent court during a summit Thursday, providing a potential hurdle to agreement on an EU growth pact, officials said. (published 0032 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: UK CONSUMERS STUCK IN DEEPEST FUNK FOR 40 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Britons have not been so gloomy about their prospects since records began 40 years ago, according to a survey released Friday. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ UPDATE: BANKING GROUP ASKS UK TO EXAMINE LIBOR PROCESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The process for setting one of the world's most important interest rates veered toward a shake-up when the U.K. banking group responsible for the rate asked government officials to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 2332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par STATE RESEARCHER: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S BACKTRACKING ON LOCAL GOVERNMENTS' DEBT ISSUES WON'T EASE RISKS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The recent move by China's legislature to backtrack on allowing local governments to sell bonds directly won't ease the risks from local government financing vehicles, the China Securities Journal reported Friday, citing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  researcher Jia Kang. (published 0038 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ UPDATE: U.S. CLEARS CHINA FROM IRAN OIL SANCTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. exempted China from penalties for doing business with Tehran as the latest set of U.S. sanctions targeting Iran's oil exports took effect on Thursday. (published 2338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  TRIMS LATIN AMERICA GROWTH FORECAST ON BRAZIL, COMMODITIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The economic outlook for Latin America has dimmed, given commodity-price declines and weakness in Brazil, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's chief economist for the region said Thursday in lowering his 2012 projection for Latin America's gross-domestic-product expansion to 3.2% from 3.8% as of March. (published 2115 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DBS GROUP TRIPLES U.S. COMMERCIAL PAPER PROGRAM TO $15 BILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DBS Group Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday said the banking group has raised the size of its existing U.S. commercial paper program to $15 billion from $5 billion at present. (published 2327 GMT) [ 29-06-12 0100GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120629e86t00020\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
