\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For June 27\b0\par\par\uc2 1,527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2012\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: NZ MAY TRADE SURPLUS NARROWS; EXPORTS, IMPORTS REMAIN RESILIENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's monthly trade surplus narrowed in May from a month earlier, reinforcing the view that the country's current account deficit is set to widen over the coming year. (published 0436 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA JULY MANUFACTURERS' OUTLOOK DIPS; BOK UNVEILS ECONOMIC SENTIMENT INDEX \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An index measuring South Korean manufacturers' outlook on business conditions for July fell for the second straight month, weighed by slower domestic demand and growing uncertainty over a solution to Europe's debt crisis, a survey by the Bank of Korea showed Wednesday. (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA TO SPUR YUAN USE IN HONG KONG - \f28 \uc2 \f2 XINHUA\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China will expand the use of the yuan in Hong Kong and promote new yuan products as part of a package of measures aimed at strengthening economic ties with the Special Administrative Region, the state-run \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xinhua News Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported Wednesday. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: YUAN DEPRECIATION PRESSURE MAY PROMPT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESEARCHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan will face "relatively big" depreciation pressure for the rest of this year and perhaps next year, possibly prompting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a researcher with the commerce ministry said. (published 0659 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA PROPOSES FUND, CREDIT TO BOOST LATAM INVESTMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the last leg of a trip through several South American nations, Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao proposed a multibillion-dollar investment fund and line of credit aimed at construction and infrastructure projects. (published 2237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RBA EXEC SAYS MINING MAY GROW TO 12% OF AUSTRALIA GDP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's resources boom may almost double the sector's contribution to national gross domestic product within five years, said John Edwards, a Reserve Bank of Australia board member. (published 0529 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA'S HENAN PROVINCE CANCELS PROPOSAL TO EASE PROPERTY MEASURES - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government of China's central province of Henan has cancelled its proposal to ease property measures, the 21st Century Business Herald reported Wednesday, citing an unnamed source from the Henan office of the state banking regulator. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF CHINA\f28 \uc2 \f2  PRESIDENT: PARTIAL INTEREST-RATE LIBERALIZATION WON'T HURT SPREAD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (3988.HK) President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Li Lihui\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday that China's recent relaxation of controls on interest rates "won't affect its spread" and is an important step toward interest-rate liberalization. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA'S BANKS TARGET AUSTRALIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese banks such as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Industrial & Commercial Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or ICBC, are muscling into Australia's syndicated loan market, seeking to replace Europe's debt-laden lenders as they retrench in the Pacific nation. (published 2341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA BANKING REGULATOR WARNS OF RISKS IN PARTNERSHIPS WITH CREDIT-GUARANTEE FIRMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's banking regulator Tuesday warned banking institutions of risks in partnerships with credit-guarantee firms. (published 0144 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: HARVEY NORMAN CEO EXPECTS A$ TO REMAIN STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A high Australian dollar exchange rate is the new reality for Australian businesses, which must adjust to survive, Katie Page, the chief executive of retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Harvey Norman Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., said Wednesday. (published 0605 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: HK SHOULD KEEP SUPPLYING NEW LAND - HANG LUNG CHAIRMAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The next Hong Kong government under Chief Executive-elect Leung Chun-ying should be able to temper the city's exuberant real-estate market by maintaining a program to supply new land that was revived under the current administration, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Lung Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (0010.HK) Chairman Ronnie Chan told Dow Jones Newswires on Wednesday. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE MAS: PRICED S$2.0 BLN 10-YEAR BONDS AT 1.55% AVERAGE YIELD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore government has priced a 2.0 billion Singapore dollar (US$1.56 billion) Sept. 1, 2022, bond issue at an average yield of 1.55%, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore said Wednesday. (published 0508 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par YIEH PHUI TO SELL 2-YEAR DIM SUM BONDS AS SOON AS THIS WEEK - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan steel maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yieh Phui Enterprise Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will sell two-year offshore yuan-denominated bonds, known as dim sum bonds, as soon as this week, a person familiar with the situation said Wednesday. (published 0154 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STANCHART: EXPECTS HIGH SINGLE-DIGIT 1H REVENUE GROWTH; WEAK \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WEIGHED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard Chartered PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects to report high single-digit revenue growth in the first half of 2012 that has slowed from double-digit growth in the same period last year because of weakness in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 --especially the Indian rupee, the bank said Wednesday. (published 0447 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: QATAR HOLDING CALLS ON \f28 \uc2 \f2 GLENCORE\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO SWEETEN OFFER FOR \f28 \uc2 \f2 XSTRATA\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sovereign-wealth fund \f28 \uc2 \f2 Qatar Holding\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which has amassed a substantial stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xstrata PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , called on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Glencore International PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Tuesday to sweeten the terms of its merger proposal with the Anglo-Swiss miner. (published 2308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: YITAI COAL SECURES US$388 MLN IN CORNERSTONE INVESTMENT FOR HK IPO - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inner Mongolia Yitai Coal Co. has secured commitments from cornerstone investors for more than a third of its up US$1.1 billion initial public offering in Hong Kong, increasing the chance that the deal will get done despite rocky markets and investor wariness toward share sales. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 KKR\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO BUY MAJORITY STAKE IN HEALTHCARE FIRM GENESIS CARE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KKR & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . L.P said Wednesday it will acquire a majority stake in closely-held Genesis Care, which provides services to patients with cancer and cardiovascular disease at public hospitals and private clinics in Australia. (published 0109 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PAL HOLDINGS\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO ISSUE 17 BLN SHARES TO HELP \f28 \uc2 \f2 PHILIPPINE AIRLINES\f28 \uc2 \f2  REFLEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PAL Holdings Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the controlling shareholder of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippine Airlines Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., said Wednesday its board has approved a plan to boost its capital stock to enable it to issue 17 billion shares to help fund the flag carrier's refleeting program. (published 0537 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN FUND MANAGER AMP BUYS INTO SELF-MANAGED PENSIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AMP Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is expanding its presence in the rapidly-expanding self-managed superannuation industry with the acquisition of part of Australia's largest SMSF administrator, Cavendish Group. (published 0036 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JUDGE ISSUES PRELIMINARY INJUNCTION AGAINST \f28 \uc2 \f2 SAMSUNG\f28 \uc2 \f2  GALAXY TAB IN US \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . was dealt a blow Tuesday when a California judge issued an injunction banning sales of the company's Galaxy Tab 10.1 touchscreen tablet at the request of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TEN NETWORK APPOINTS SIOBHAN MCKENNA TO BOARD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ten Network Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it has appointed Siobhan McKenna as a director of the company. (published 2349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES HIGHER BEFORE EUROPEAN UNION SUMMIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian markets were higher Wednesday ahead of a forthcoming European Union summit, with Hong Kong and China leading gains on speculation of stronger financial ties between China and Hong Kong. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN LAW TO REINSURE IRANIAN CRUDE TANKERS TOOK EFFECT TODAY -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan has passed a law that allows the government to provide insurance coverage of up to $7.6 billion for tankers carrying Iranian crude oil to Japanese ports, said a spokesman with the marine department of the country's transportation ministry, adding that the law took effect Wednesday. (published 0647 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM PROTESTS CNOOC'S MOVE TO OFFER 9 BLOCKS IN SOUTH CHINA SEA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam late Tuesday launched a formal protest against \f28 \uc2 \f2 China National Offshore Oil Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s move to offer nine blocks in the South China Sea for joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with foreign companies, stating that the blocks are in Vietnamese waters. (published 0422 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA EXPECTS RECORD RESOURCE EXPORT EARNINGS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian earnings from mineral and energy exports are expected to jump 8% to a record 209.5 billion Australian dollars next fiscal year as commodity prices bounce back, a government report Wednesday said. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BHP EXPECTS SUBSTANTIAL UPLIFT IN ESCONDIDA OUTPUT IN JUNE QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it expects production at Chilean copper mine Escondida to show a substantial uplift in the June quarter, helping the world's largest copper mine meet production guidance for the fiscal year after it was disrupted by a strike. (published 2309 GMT Tuesday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA GOVT PANEL RECOMMENDS MAJOR CHANGES IN DIESEL SUBSIDY SYSTEM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A top-level Indian government panel has recommended an overhaul of the nation's diesel subsidy system, which could partially free up the price of the fuel and address a major worry about India's economic future. (published 0656 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA JANUARY-MAY DISTILLERS GRAIN IMPORTS RISE 41.5% -CNGOIC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's imports of distillers dried grains with solubles, or DDGS, rose 41.5% in the first five months of this year to 913,000 metric tons, the state-backed China National Grain and Oils Information Center said Wednesday. (published 0210 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA STEEL WORKS TO SUPPLY STEEL BARS, BILLETS TO TRAFIGURA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Integrated steel company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malaysia Steel Works Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or Masteel, said Wednesday that it will supply up to 270,000 metric tons of steel billets and bars to major commodity trader Trafigura Pte. over the next three years. (published 0648 GMT) [ 27-06-12 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120627e86r000d1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
