\par\par \b \uc2 Midpoint drags yuan up slightly; dollar demand firm\b0\par\par\uc2 461 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2012\par 07:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 PBOC\uc2  wants market to test wider band\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen if depreciation goes too far\par \par \uc2 By Gabriel Wildau\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, June 14 (Reuters) - A strong fixing from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dragged the yuan slightly higher on Thursday, but traders still say yuan sellers outnumber buyers in the face of the euro zone debt crisis and a slowing domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 The yuan changed hands at 6.3675 per dollar at midday, 16 pips stronger than Wednesday's close, but the slight rise occurred after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its midpoint at 6.3791, 80 pips weaker than Friday's close.\par \par \uc2 "The midpoint was set pretty low, but the transaction prices aren't very different from yesterday, which means that the market is still short (the yuan)," said a trader at a foreign bank in Guangzhou.\par \par \uc2 Spot yuan has traded weaker than the midpoint fixing nearly every day since mid-March and weakened nearly 1 percent in May, its largest monthly fall ever.\par \par \uc2 The midpoint fixing is the base rate that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses to flag the government's intentions for the yuan's value, and from which the yuan is allowed rise or fall by 1 percent.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has appeared content to let the yuan fall in line with the strength of the dollar globally amid a flight to safety spurred by the eurozone debt crisis and sluggish growth in both the U.S. and China.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  doubled the yuan's daily allowable trading band in mid-April to 1.0 percent from 0.5 percent in a move to allow market forces to play a bigger role in setting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value.\par \par \uc2 But there are limits to how much yuan weakness the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will allow. The foreign bank trader said he saw clear signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday to strengthen the yuan.\par \par \uc2 On that day, the yuan touched 6.3782 - near a six-month low - in early morning trade, before strengthening sharply in late morning and afternoon to close at 6.3681.\par \par \uc2 Traders also say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been using the daily fixing to encourage the market to test the boundaries of the expanded trading limit.\par \par \uc2 "You can see two days ago they set the midpoint higher by about 100 pips, today they set it lower by about 100 pips. This is the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  testing daily volatility," said a trader at a major state-owned bank in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 In the offshore market, offshore yuan (CNH) traded at 6.3675, in line with the spot rate.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Eric Meijer)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN-MIDDAY | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120617e86e0001k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
