\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For May 3\b0\par\par\uc2 1,495 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2012\par 09:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: GEITHNER: YUAN NEEDS TO RISE MORE VS DOLLAR, OTHER \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Timothy Geithner\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday the yuan should continue to rise against the dollar, even as he acknowledged China has moved toward a more market-based exchange rate system and eased controls on capital flows. (published 0430 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US OFFICIAL: CHINA'S YUAN STILL MISALIGNED DESPITE RECENT APPRECIATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Beijing for the U.S.-China Strategic and Economic Dialogue, the official said the yuan has risen "very substantially" since 2005, but added "further progress is needed." The U.S. believes that as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reduces \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the market will naturally reduce the misalignment, the official said. (published 0700 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ UPDATE: CHINA APPEARS MORE WILLING TO DISCUSS NEEDED REFORMS - US SENIOR OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese officials appear more willing than before to discuss far-reaching economic reforms that the U.S. believes are needed to rebalance the global economy, including easing restrictions on foreign ownership of financial sector firms and boosting the dividends that Chinese state-owned industries are required to pay, a senior U.S. official said. (published 0609 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ADB WARNS OF SEVERE IMPACT ON DEVELOPING ASIA IF EUROPE CRISIS WORSENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe's sovereign debt crisis, if it worsens, could have a more severe impact on developing Asia and the crisis that may ensue--likely transmitted first through the closely intertwined global financial system--would last longer, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asian Development Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  warned in a study released Thursday. (published 0058 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA, JAPAN, CHINA TO INCREASE MUTUAL BOND INVESTMENT, SHARE INFORMATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China, Japan, and South Korea said Thursday they agreed to use their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves to increase investments in the treasury bonds of the three Asian nations and establish a framework to share information about these investments, in a move to maintain stability in their financial markets. (published 0239 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN SERVICES SECTORS SLUMP ROUNDS OUT GLUM ECONOMIC PICTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's services industry recorded its most severe slump in three years in April, adding to the increasing list of weak sectors in the economy and validating the decision this week for a hefty cut in interest rates by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: ECONOMISTS PUSH OUT NZ RATE EXPECTATIONS AS JOBS DATA DISAPPOINT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A rise in New Zealand's unemployment rate, coupled with weaker home sales and recent falls in agricultural commodity prices, has seen economists push back expectations for when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will start hiking rates. (published 0331 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  OFFERS CNY65 BLN REVERSE REPOS TO BOOST LIQUIDITY - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday offered CNY65 billion of seven-day reverse repurchase agreements to selected banks, a move aimed at improving liquidity in the banking system to cope with a slowing economy, three traders participating in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  told Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0329 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES AT RECORD HIGH OF $316.84B AT END-APRIL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves rose for a fourth straight month to a record high in April due to gains in the value of non-U.S. dollar assets and higher returns on investments, the Bank of Korea said Thursday. (published 2101 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NORWAY'S SOVEREIGN WEALTH FUND MULLING $400M INVESTMENT IN S KOREAN SECURITIES -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Norwegian sovereign wealth fund Government Pension Fund Global is considering a $400 million investment in South Korean securities, Maeil Business Newspaper reported Thursday, citing unnamed sources in the securities industry. (published 0002 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: TEMASEK RAISES US$2.48 BLN VIA \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , CCB SHARE SALES; STAYS BULLISH ON CHINA BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore state-investment firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Temasek Holdings Pte. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . raised US$2.48 billion by selling portions of stakes it holds in Chinese lenders \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and China Construction Bank Ltd. via placements priced at the low end of indicative ranges, as markets remain choppy, people familiar with the situation said Thursday. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA PROSECUTORS QUESTIONING LG DISPLAY EMPLOYEES OVER POSSIBLE OLED TECHNOLOGY INFRINGEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Flat-panel maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG Display Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . employees are being investigated over alleged infringement of rival Samsung Mobile Display's ultra-thin technology, South Korean prosecutors revealed Thursday. (published 0648 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ELPIDA BONDHOLDERS MAY OPPOSE SALE OF COMPANY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A group of Elpida Memory Inc. bondholders said they are concerned about the failed Japanese chip maker being sold at an "undervalued" price in an auction closing this week, and are considering submitting their own alternative reorganization plan for the company. (published 0434 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: WESTPAC REPORTS RECORD CASH EARNINGS AMID SUBDUED MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . reported record first-half cash earnings for the second time in a row, even as the lender struggled to preserve profit margins amid slowing loan growth and higher funding costs. (published 0210 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FELDA GLOBAL PLANS TO SELL IPO SHARES TO INDIGENOUS MALAYSIANS AT MYR4.65/SHR -GOVT NOTICE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysian state-controlled palm-oil plantation company Felda Global Ventures Holdings Bhd. plans to sell 419.5 million shares that have been allocated to indigenous Malaysians at MYR4.65/share, ahead of its initial public offering that aims to raise more than $3 billion, according to a government notice. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CBA'S 40 BPS RATE CUT BEATS NAB, PRESSURES PEERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday became the second of Australia's four biggest lenders to pass on part of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's 50-basis-point rate cut to its customers, adding pressure on the remaining two to follow suit. (published 0328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par YGM TRADING: IN EXCLUSIVE TALKS TO BUY UK AQUASCUTUM'S BUSINESS, ASSETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 YGM Trading Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., which bought the license for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aquascutum\f28 \uc2 \f2  luxury clothing brand for 42 markets in Asia in 2009, said Wednesday it has entered exclusive talks with the administrators of U.K. luxury fashion retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aquascutum\f28 \uc2 \f2  over the potential acquisition of its business and assets. (published 0303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASCENDAS REIT SEEKS TO RAISE UP TO S$306M VIA PRIVATE PLACEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ascendas Real Estate Investment Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday said it is seeking to raise S$298.5 million to S$306 million through a private placement of new units to institutional investors. (published 2346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 KOREAN AIR\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO FOCUS ON PROFITABILITY AFTER 1Q NET LOSS ON HIGH OIL COSTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With high oil prices to persist into the second quarter \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korean Air Lines\f28 \uc2 \f2  is rethinking schedules and aircraft deployment as it looks to "focus on profitability," it said Thursday after swinging to a first-quarter net loss. (published 0545 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: HARVEY NORMAN ISSUES PROFIT WARNING; DISCOUNTING, A$ HIT MARGINS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Electricals and furniture retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Harvey Norman Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that it expects pretax profit for the nine months to March 31 to drop 25%, as discounting by competitors and a high Australian dollar hit margins. (published 0601 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FIRST GEN SETS DIVIDEND RATE ON NEW PREFERRED SHARES AT 7.7808% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 First Gen Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it has set the dividend rate on new preferred shares it will sell next week at 7.7808%. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ABBOTT TIES UP WITH \f28 \uc2 \f2 BIOCON\f28 \uc2 \f2  UNIT TO DEVELOP NUTRITION PRODUCTS IN INDIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. drug maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Abbott Laboratories\f28 \uc2 \f2  has tied up with a unit of Indian biotechnology company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Biocon Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to set up a research and development center for nutrition products. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES DROP ON WEAK US, EUROPE DATA; CYCLICALS STRUGGLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Most Asian stock markets were lower Thursday after disappointing data from Europe and the U.S. revived concerns about the global economic outlook, hurting exporters. (published 0425 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALASKA SENATOR PITCHES NATURAL GAS EXPORTS TO JAPANESE OFFICIALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sen. Lisa Murkowski is pitching her state to Japanese officials as a source of natural gas that can replace the nuclear power taken offline in the wake of the Fukushima Daiichi power plant disaster. (published 2136 GMT Wednesday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA NEEDS URGENT GREENHOUSE GAS MEASURES TO MEET TARGETS -WORLD BANK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China needs to accelerate efforts to meet its own targets for reducing greenhouse gas emissions, particularly by introducing new measures in its fast-growing cities, the World Bank said Thursday. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HANWHA SOLARONE TO SUPPLY 5.6MW SOLAR MODULES TO JAPAN'S \f28 \uc2 \f2 SOFTBANK\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hanwha Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday that its affiliate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hanwha SolarOne Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has been selected as the supplier of solar modules worth 5.6 megawatts for Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Softbank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0242 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RIO TINTO\f28 \uc2 \f2  CONTINUES TO EYE LONG-TERM DEMAND FOR COMMODITIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is holding fast to expectations of continued long-term demand for its metals and minerals, with the appetite for copper in particular forecast to increasingly outstrip the global supplies over the coming years, Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tom Albanese\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0003 GMT) [ 03-05-12 0710GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120503e853000fn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
