\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ PBOC Chief: Risk From Widened Yuan Trading Band Manageable - Report\b0\par\par\uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2012\par 03:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 22 Apr 2012 21:41 EDT *DJ  PBOC Chief: \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  To \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Less In Market - Report\par \par \uc2 22 Apr 2012 21:42 EDT DJ  PBOC Chief: Risk From Widened Yuan Trading Band Manageable - Report\par \par \uc2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)-China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a number of tools to manage its exchange rate and the risks from the yuan's newly widened trading band are manageable, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Zhou Xiaochuan was quoted as saying in a report.\par \par \uc2 Zhou said in an interview with Caijing magazine that in future, the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less frequently in the market and its actions would be more flexible.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also has a variety of means to administer and regulate the exchange rate when necessary. So the risks are manageable," he said in the magazine's latest issue, out Monday.\par \par \uc2 The PBOC sets a daily rate for the yuan against the dollar--known as the parity level--and then allows a trading band which is now 1% above and below that level. The band was widened one week ago from 0.5% above or below the parity rate, where it had been since 2007.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market while it has other administrative measures that can affect supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the market exchange rate moves beyond the specified range. Future \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be less frequent and more flexible," Zhou said.\par \par \uc2 Zhou repeated past statements that the yuan is nearing "equilibrium" or fair value and that has made it easier to move ahead with reforms of the exchange-rate mechanism.\par \par \uc2 He said the impact on the export sector would be determined by the ability of exporters to adjust their products, but noted the move also sends a signal that there should be less investment in export capacity and more in the services sector over the medium to long term.\par \par \uc2 The PBOC chief also said it was time to try to promote more market-oriented interest rates, though he suggested this issue still faced obstacles.\par \par \uc2 "Right now, externally, the global financial crisis has not subsided, while internally there is danger of an economic slowdown and inflation in China. Hence, we need to wait for the appropriate time to see if we can reach a consensus," he said.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sets guidelines for banks on lending rates and it has a cap on deposit rates, effectively setting those rates.\par \par \uc2 Zhou suggested a cautious approach to interest-rate liberalization--first expanding lending rates.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, a market benchmark interest-rate system should be fostered to improve the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest-rate regulatory mechanism and help financial institutions raise their pricing power over interest rates, he said.\par \par \uc2 Zhou said that work on a deposit insurance system was in progress, as was an "exit mechanism" for failed financial institutions.\par \par \uc2 China has been considering allowing private capital in its state-dominated banking system but it has moved slowly, partly due to fear of potential bank failures, particularly with no deposit insurance system in effect.\par \par \uc2 Zhou said interest-rate liberalization could be reached over a transitional period, though he did not offer any estimate of the length of that period.\par \par \uc2 He also suggested, however, that might not have to wait for all conditions to be ready.\par \par \uc2 "While we need to take all factors into consideration when driving forward interest-rate and exchange-rate reform, I don't think we should wait until all conditions are fully mature to promote the reform."\par \par \uc2 -By William Kazer; Dow Jones Newswires (8610) 8400 - 7706; william.kazer@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 22, 2012 21:42 ET (01:42 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120423e84n00168\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
