\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Trader Bets On $5 \uc2 Groupon\uc2  After IPO Lockup Expiry\b0\par\par\uc2 1,385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 2012\par 17:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 11:28 (Dow Jones) It looks like one trader expects a $5 price on \uc2 Groupon\uc2  (GRPN) come July. Activity in GRPN options surged Tuesday as the put-call ratio soared to 16.2-1, more than twice the previous high. The most-actively traded contract was a bet that GRPN shares--currently trading at $12.69 after earlier hitting a post-IPO low of $12.25--could tumble to around $5 by July 21. There were 4K July $5 puts bought for 25c each. The trade could be a bet on a plunge after GRPN's IPO lockup expires June 1, a move that could flood the market with new shares. Just 6% of the Class A shares outstanding were sold to the public as part of November's IPO. (kaitlyn.kiernan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:20 (Dow Jones) The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought notes due between February 2036 and February 2042. Dealers put up $4.843 billion for sale. The buying isn't inspiring much of a comeback in the market today, with prices near session lows on optimism, at least for today, that the euro-zone economy is getting by. Benchmark 10-year notes down 10/32 to bring their yield back above 2%. The 30-year bond down 24/32 to yield 3.152%. (cynthia.lin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:18 (Dow Jones) Canada dollar's rally appears to be running out of steam as it falls below the 0.9875 level, said CIBC's Don Mikolich. "The USD/CAD had a decent rally for the day, but familiar technical levels remain in sight for a while," Mikolich said, noting the 0.9838 March low as a key support level. USD/CAD down 1.21% on Tuesday, largely driven by the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  delivering a hawkish tone in its policy statement while it left rates unchanged. Mikolich notes that Wednesday's MPR report from the \uc2 BOC\uc2  and Friday's CPI numbers could "flush out" a stronger CAD or, alternatively, send the loonie back to parity against the USD. USD/CAD at 0.9867, according to CQG. (david.george-cosh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:18 (Dow Jones) Big night for tech earnings, with Intel (INTC), \uc2 IBM\uc2 , \uc2 Yahoo\uc2  (YHOO) and Seagate (STX) posting quarterly results after the close. INTC will give investors a glimpse into PC and server demand, and analysts expect revenue in line with INTC's forecast. Hard-drive maker STX, meanwhile, should provide details about how a recovery from severe flooding in Thailand is progressing. \uc2 IBM\uc2  should be a good barometer for business spending on tech. As for YHOO, investors simply looking for more details on its turnaround strategy. All four stocks up amid broad market rally. (shara.tibken@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:17 (Dow Jones) GOL shares jump on a report that Brazil may reduce payroll taxes for the airline industry. The move, which would be partially offset by a tax on revenue, is likely to add about 14% to Ebitda for GOL and rival TAM, says \uc2 UBS\uc2 . It adds that GOL is up 8.7% versus TAM's 1.2% advance stems from GOL slumping to a 6-month low Monday, capping a 1/3 stock tumble the past month in Brazil. TAM shares have been supported, says \uc2 UBS\uc2 , by the company's soon-to-close merger with Chile's LAN (LFL). (paulo.winterstein@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:16 (Dow Jones) If the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  fails to ease monetary policy further at its meeting next week, that could lead to a quick unwind of yen shorts that have built up to multi-year highs in recent weeks, says Yujiro Goto at Nomura Securities. Even if the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  announces just a small addition to its bond-buying program, that might still disappoint the market that is shaping up to expect another round of sizeable stimulus, Goto says. The dollar is higher against the yen Tuesday, but has been falling over the past couple of weeks even as traders build up anti-yen bets. The dollar is at Y80.69 from Y80.41 late Monday, according to EBS via CQG. (stephen.bernard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:07 (Dow Jones) A widening trading band for the Chinese yuan means less \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, says Blackrock Investment Institute's Ewen Cameron Watt. That will lessen China's need to buy dollars and US Treasurys, while China also works to diversify its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, he says. While Blackrock believes that China will buy fewer Treasurys, the country still won't be "aggressive sellers," giving support to the "low for long" US rates view, he adds. (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:05 (Dow Jones) The clarion calls for the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  to hike rates will be loud today, but RBC's Dawn Desjardins says there remain several global and domestic uncertainties working to counterbalance the bank's improved growth outlook for Canada. Europe's fiscal difficulties, moderating growth in the emerging economies and develeraging in the US are all factors that will weigh on the BoC when deciding whether to hike rates either in 2012 or in 2013 (as is widely expected). Desjardins says those "persistent gyrations in financial markets" need to have abated before policymakers are confident to move the overnight target rate away from its current level of 1.00%. (david.george-cosh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:02 (Dow Jones) Tuesday's industrial-production data and yesterday's Empire State manufacturing index indicate the pace of factory activity tailed off toward the end of 1Q, says \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 . "Factory output looks to have run a little bit ahead of sales, and an inventory re-balancing may be under way." (jeffrey.sparshott@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:59 (Dow Jones) State Street (STT) may have missed 1Q earnings estimates, but Evercore sees some bright spots. Yes, higher compensation is an issue--the compensation-to-revenue ratio rose to 44% from 40.6%. But STT assures it's targeting a full-year figure of 39.2%, predicated on higher revenue. Evercore also notes results in some instances exceeded its expectations; for instance, spread revenue topped views on higher net interest margin. Also, excluding fair-value adjustments, STT's core fees slightly edged Evercore's estimate, a result of higher market valuations and net new business. Shares are up 1.4% at $44.29, roughly in line with the broader market's advance. (corrie.driebusch@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:57 (Dow Jones) The power sector is a driver of world copper demand, in the form of the heavy duty power cables electrifying rural China and in wiring in homes and office buildings worldwide. It's ironic, then, that the same industry threatens to undercut the ability of the world's top copper miner to produce the metal. Codelco CEO Diego Hernandez warns that skyrocketing power prices, more energy-intensive mining, and an unreliable grid threaten to make Chile's copper industry less competitive. The energy intensity of Codelco's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  is projected to increase by a quarter by 2017, he says, and power prices have nearly tripled since 2000. (matt.day@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:50 (Dow Jones) Consumer-discretionary names, which have been some of the biggest advancers so far in 2012, are lagging in today's market rebound. Three of the 5 largest decliners in the S&P 500 come from that space, led by \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  (SBUX). It has been undergoing its first pullback of any significance since November; after that, the stock had surged 52% to all-time highs. Still, shares are still up 27% in 2012 and 4.5% in April despite a 2.1% decline today. Also lagging is restaurant chain Darden (DRI), which is off 1.2%. It has been retreating the past month after getting back toward a record high a month ago. Then there's ad-agency owner \uc2 Omnicom\uc2  (OMC), which is off 2.1% despite a modest 1Q beat. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Equities Market Talk Editors, \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Paul Vigna, 212 416-2184,paul.vigna@dowjones.com \par Visit the Market Talk website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 04-17-12 1128ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120417e84h000d7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
