\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico, Chile pesos gain on China, US data\b0\par\par\uc2 613 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2012\par 18:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso gains 0.7 percent; Brazil real off 0.31 percent\par \par \uc2 * Real underperformed in 1st quarter, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears weigh\par \par \uc2 * Chile peso gains 1.06 percent, copper up 1 percent\par \par \uc2 By Caroline Stauffer\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, April 2 (Reuters) - The Mexican and Chilean pesos strengthened on Monday after manufacturing data from the world's two largest economies beat forecasts, though Brazil's real weakened on "the specter of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Data showed new factory orders in \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to an 11-month high in March while growth in U.S. manufacturing surpassed economists' expectations in February.\par \par \uc2 China and the United States are Latin America's top trade partners. The price of metals such as copper, exported by many Latin American countries, rose after the manufacturing data pointed to sustained demand from the world's economic giants.\par \par \uc2 "The data showed growth is generally holding up reasonably well, commodities prices are making significant gains," said Nick Chamie, head of emerging markets research at RBC Securities in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso gained the most out of the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ending 1.06 percent stronger to bid 483.1 per U.S. dollar. That was its strongest close in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 Copper for delivery in three months rose 1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Chile gets more than half of its export earnings from the red metal, a key component in electrical and electronic equipment.\par \par \uc2 "This was a completely favorable scenario for the peso," said one trader in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had weakened for the five previous sessions, gained 0.7 percent to 12.7281 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso is particularly sensitive to U.S. manufacturing data as many Mexicans work in U.S. factories and the United States buys nearly 80 percent of Mexico's exports by value.\par \par \uc2 REAL BUCKS TREND\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real, however, weakened 0.31 percent to close bidding 1.8277 per dollar. Government measures to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and data showing the pace of manufacturing in Brazil had slowed for a third straight month weighed.\par \par \uc2 "The ongoing specter of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the part of the government is the key reason," said RBC's Chamie.\par \par \uc2 "We also had a weaker-than-expected PMI," he said, referring to Markit's Brazil Manufacturing Purchasing Manager's Index.\par \par \uc2 The index edged down to 51.1 last month from 51.4 in February.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  often purchases dollars in the spot market on days the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is strengthening as policymakers aim to weaken the real in an effort to make Brazil's manufacturing exports more competitive.\par \par \uc2 The government has also raised its financial transactions or "IOF" tax and on March 12 extended its scope to foreign debt maturing in up to five years. Some traders have sold the real fearing the government could take additional measures like extending the tax to all financial transactions.\par \par \uc2 Investors are also down on the real because Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to lower interest rates in coming months. That would curb potential returns in Brazil as economic growth slows.\par \par \uc2 "Even if they aren't introducing new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures, these are all factors that will restrain the real," said Nicholas Bennenbroek, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "Chile has had one of the stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because inflation is favorable and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not likely to cut rates," he added.\par \par \uc2 The real strengthened 2.17 percent in the first quarter of 2012, reaching just a third of the Chilean peso's gains.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Froilan Romero in Santiago)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120405e8420013a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
