\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-China c.bank study outlines capital reform roadmap\b0\par\par\uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2012\par 01:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * PBOC report says it's good time to open up capital account\par \par \uc2 * PBOC report says housing, capital mkts to fully open in 5-10 yrs\par \par \uc2 * PBOC report not a policy announcement, indicates reform debate\par \par \uc2 (Updates with details direct from report, context)\par \par \uc2 BEIJING, Feb 23 (Reuters) - China should seize the opportunity to free-up capital account controls as the rewards of liberalisation outweigh the risks, said a report by the People's Bank of China statistics department published on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The reforms should take place over the next five to 10 years and give foreigners more freedom to buy Chinese property, stocks and bonds at the same time as allowing direct access by Chinese nationals to overseas property and asset markets, it said.\par \par \uc2 The report, although not a policy announcement, provides one of the most detailed roadmaps yet of capital account reform from a government institution, underlining the high level debate underway in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 China should take advantage of what the report called "a period of strategic opportunity" for opening up its capital markets, giving Chinese firms the chance to buy Western companies at bargain prices with stock valuations in many cases depressed by successive international financial crises.\par \par \uc2 The report argued that China should free-up the capital account in three stages, the first in one to three years allowing more outbound investment.\par \par \uc2 The second step, in three to five years, would see Chinese banks lending yuan to overseas borrowers with overseas yuan holders also able to lend yuan in the mainland market.\par \par \uc2 The opening of housing, bond and stock investments is the third step, after which derivatives and other asset markets could be opened.\par \par \uc2 But it advocated that China permanently keep control of some items, including short-term foreign debt.\par \par \uc2 Chinese government officials, including the head of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchdog, have repeatedly said there is no timetable to make the yuan convertible under the capital account, though analysts expect most controls to go by 2020.\par \par \uc2 SWIFT ACTION URGED\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's research team argues for a swifter move.\par \par \uc2 "If we want to see a free interest rate system, a free exchange rate regime, and an international yuan before opening up the capital account, we may never find the right timing," the report said.\par \par \uc2 "We must be cautious in opening up the capital account, but that does not mean we must wait endlessly," it added.\par \par \uc2 Beijing has been wary of giving too much freedom to private investments abroad.\par \par \uc2 The local government of Wenzhou, a cradle of private enterprise in China, decided in early 2011 to let local residents make direct investment abroad, but the central government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  swiftly to call an end to it.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also maintained tight control over capital flows, only permitting portfolio flows under a quota system dubbed the Qualified Foreign Institutional Investor (QFII) scheme for inflows and outflows under a programme called the Qualified Domestic Institutional Investor (QDII) scheme.\par \par \uc2 Those controls have helped shield China from some of the impact of global financial turmoil, but they also constrict the flow of capital to where it is needed, even as the country has amassed the world's biggest store \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 China has about $3.2 trillion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. In 2011, it chalked up a current account surplus of $201.1 billion, the State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SAFE) said earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Liberalising controls would promote the shift from labour-intensive to more value-added industries, and encourage domestic consumption by giving households more avenues to invest and accumulate wealth, said the PBOC study.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Chris Buckley and Zhou Xin; Editing by Nick Edwards)\par \par \uc2 CHINA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /REFORM (UPDATE 1) | ABX | ABN | C | GRO | MTL | SOF | D | E | RBN | M | O | OIL | Z | RNP | DNP | PCM | PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120223e82n0006o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
