\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 762 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2012\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: JAPAN HARDENS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RHETORIC AS YEN NEARS RECORD HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister said Thursday he cannot "overlook" speculative moves in the market to push the yen higher, stepping up his warnings over the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's renewed strength as it threatens to exacerbate the nation's trade shortfalls and economic slowdown. (published 0434 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ YAMAGUCHI SAYS BANK READY TO ACT AS GLOBAL RISKS REMAIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The deputy governor of the Bank of Japan said Thursday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stands ready to take action as the European debt crisis and the strong yen continue to pose a threat to the economy and financial markets. (published 0414 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA DEC TRADE SURPLUS WIDENS AS MINING EXPORTS BOOM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's trade surplus accelerated in December buoyed by mining exports to Asia but economists said softening commodities prices mean that trade may have peaked. (published 0350 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FINANCE MINISTER: ECONOMY SHOWING SOME WEAKNESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's finance minister, Bahk Jae-wan, said Thursday that the economy is showing some weakness amid deteriorating external conditions. (published 0012 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES RISE TO 5-MONTH HIGH IN JANUARY - BOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves rose to their highest level in five months in January due to gains in the value of non-U.S. dollar assets and higher returns on investments, the Bank of Korea said Thursday. (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBI SUBBARAO: BEST TO BE UNPREDICTABLE IN TACTICAL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MANAGEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor said Thursday it is best to be unpredictable in tactical \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  management, reiterating the bank's policy of not disclosing details of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  REGULATOR: COMPLETED PREPARATIONS FOR PLANNED HONG KONG-LINKED ETFS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has completed preparatory work for launching exchange traded funds linked to Hong Kong-listed shares, Guo Shuqing, chairman of the country's securities regulator, said in an editorial published in the state-run China Securities Journal on Thursday. (published 0240 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INTERVIEW: AUSTRALIA'S FUTURE FUND EYES EUROPEAN ASSETS-EXEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Assets in Europe are on the list of investments liked by advisers to Australia's Future Fund, the country's quasi-sovereign wealth fund with 73.1 billion Australian dollars under management, according to its chairman David Murray. (published 0309 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI DEPUTY PM: NEXT FY BUDGET DEFICIT TO NARROW FROM THB400B THIS FY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's Deputy Prime Minister and Finance Minister Kittiratt Na Ranong said Thursday that the government is working on an expenditure plan for next year, which targets a narrower deficit than the THB400 billion planned for the current fiscal year ending Sept. 30. (published 0406 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: VIETNAM JAN INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION INDEX DOWN 12.9% ON MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's industrial production index fell 12.9% in January from a month earlier due to a week-long Lunar New Year holiday in the month, the General Statistics Office said Thursday. (published 0409 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: VIETNAM JANUARY TRADE DEFICIT NARROWS TO $100M VS $269M IN DEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's trade deficit in January narrowed to $100 million from $269 million in December, with both imports and exports falling significantly, the General Statistics Office said Thursday. (published 0405 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM JANUARY RETAIL SALES UP 22% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's retail sales of goods and services in January rose 22% from a year earlier to VND191 trillion, the General Statistics Office said Thursday. (published 0413 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S RBA APPOINTS CHRISTOPHER KENT ASSISTANT GOVERNOR ECONOMIC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday that Christopher Kent will be its next Assistant Governor, a post widely viewed as a stepping stone to being a future head of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0412 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 NEW CHINA LIFE INSURANCE\f28 \uc2 \f2  PLANS CNY15 BLN BOND SALES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New China Life Insurance Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it plans to raise CNY15 billion through debt issuance, making it the latest Chinese insurer to undertake a fundraising campaign to shore up its growth prospects. (published 0137 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA DEVELOPMENT BANK: TO SELL CNY40 BLN BONDS TUESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Development Bank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it plans to auction CNY20 billion of five-year fixed-rate bonds and CNY20 billion of 10-year floating-rate bonds on the interbank market Tuesday. (published 0122 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par LOTTE SHOPPING PLANS TO SELL 3-YEAR OFFSHORE YUAN BOND - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean department store operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lotte Shopping Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is selling a three-year offshore yuan-denominated bond, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Thursday. (published 0402 GMT) [ 02-02-12 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120202e822000ao\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
