\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 528 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2012\par 13:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EFSF FINDING SOLID DEMAND FOR THREE-YEAR BOND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro zone's temporary rescue fund has found solid demand from investors for its three-year bond Thursday, in a debt sale that comes as one of the first tests for the European rescue project in 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPAIN, ITALY DEBT INSURANCE COSTS RISE AMID EURO-ZONE CONCERNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The cost of insuring Spanish and Italian debt against default was higher in early trading Thursday as ongoing concerns about the euro-zone debt crisis continue to put pressure on credit default swaps levels.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPAIN BANKS STOCKS FALL AS GOVERNMENT SAYS MORE PROVISIONS NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spanish banking stocks fell in early trade Thursday after the government said the sector will need to raise about EUR50 billion in additional provisions to deal with bad property assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK PRIVATE SECTOR STRENGTHENS IN DECEMBER, STAGNANT IN 4Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K.'s private sector grew at the strongest rate for five months in December, but the economy still stagnated in the fourth quarter as a whole, financial information firm Markit said Thursday in a roundup of its closely-watched monthly surveys of services, manufacturing, and construction firms.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HUNGARY IMF NEGOTIATOR STEPS IN TO PULL HUNGARY BACK FROM BRINK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Coming under intensifying financial pressure, Hungary signaled Thursday that it was open to negotiating a standby loan with the International Monetary Fund without setting any pre-conditions, in an effort to bring Hungary back from the brink of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HUNGARY SOVEREIGN DEBT INSURANCE COSTS HIT NEW RECORD WIDES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The cost of insuring Hungarian debt against default rose to a new high for the third consecutive day Thursday amid heightened concerns the government's unorthodox policies will derail the progress of a new financial agreement with the International Monetary Fund.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN STATE OF HESSEN TO PRICE EUR1B 2017 BOND AT SWAPS +0.07 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The German state of Hessen is to price its EUR1 billion bond maturing Feb. 2017 at seven basis points over midswaps, one of the banks running the deal said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN GOVT OFFICIAL: TO KEEP BUYING EFSF BONDS WHILE WATCHING EUROPE EFFORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's government plans to make additional purchases of bonds to be issued by Europe's bailout fund, a Japanese government official said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH CONSUMER CONFIDENCE REMAINS LOW IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French consumer confidence remained low in December around levels last seen during France's 2008 to 2009 recession, statistics agency Insee said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA COMMERCE MINISTER: 2011 TRADE SURPLUS ABOUT $160 BLN - XINHUA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's trade surplus likely further narrowed last year to around $160 billion, Xinhua news agency on Thursday cited Commerce Minister Chen Deming as saying.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EX-PBOC ADVISER: YUAN WOULD NOT RISE SHARPLY IF PBOC HALTS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese yuan is not likely to rise significantly, and may even depreciate, if the People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stops \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market, a former \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IRISH JOBS MINISTER: IRELAND ATTRACTING INVESTMENTS DESPITE DEBT CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ireland faces a "massive" employment challenge but is still attracting large amounts of investment despite the euro debt crisis, Jobs Minister Richard Bruton said Thursday. [ 05-01-12 1206GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120105e815000ns\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
