\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For January 5\b0\par\par\uc2 1,888 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2012\par 08:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA GOVT: KEY INDICATORS SOFTER; INFLATION UNCERTAINTIES LINGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Ministry of Strategy and Finance on Thursday repeated its warning about growing economic uncertainty, citing risks posed by the euro-zone sovereign debt crisis and political instability in the Middle East. (published 0118 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC SUSPENDS THURSDAY'S OPEN MARKET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suspended its regular open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday, thereby injecting funds into the market in Beijing's latest attempt to provide support to the country's slowing economy, people familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: HK BUSINESS ACTIVITY CONTRACTS FOR 5TH STRAIGHT MONTH IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business activity in Hong Kong contracted for the fifth straight month in December due to the slowdown in the global economy, though it sill showed improvement from the previous month as new orders increased for the first time since July, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA COMMERCE MINISTER: 2011 TRADE SURPLUS ABOUT $160 BLN - XINHUA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's trade surplus likely further narrowed last year to around $160 billion, Xinhua news agency on Thursday cited Commerce Minister Chen Deming as saying. (published 0449 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EX-PBOC ADVISER: YUAN WOULD NOT RISE SHARPLY IF PBOC HALTS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese yuan is not likely to rise significantly, and may even depreciate, if the People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stops \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market, a former \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser said Thursday. (published 0419 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA FOOD INFLATION -3.36%, NEGATIVE FIRST TIME IN YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's wholesale price index for food articles fell 3.36% from a year earlier in the week ended Dec. 24, the first time that the food inflation rate has slipped into negative territory in several years. (published 0619 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S GOKARN: WILL RESPOND STRONGLY TO ANY SHARP ONE-WAY MOVES IN RUPEE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stands ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to smooth any sharp moves in the rupee, which is expected to stabilize now after falling sharply last year, a senior \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  official said Thursday. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S GOKARN: CURRENT RUPEE VALUATION MOVING TOWARD NEUTRALITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India Deputy Governor Subir Gokarn said Thursday that measures the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  took last year to stabilize the rupee's price action appear to be working and that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now appears be moving toward a more neutral valuation. (published 0424 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA'S RECORD BORROWING REINFORCES FISCAL WOES BUT RATING UNAFFECTED - RATING FIRMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's latest increase to its market borrowing plan reinforces concerns over the government's worsening fiscal health but it doesn't merit a rating downgrade yet as growing private savings will help partly bridge the budgetary shortfall, rating firms Fitch and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. (published 0616 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA TRADE SURPLUS SHOWS SIGNS OF COOLING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's trade surplus fell short of expectations during November, reflecting slower demand from Asia-based customers and underscoring the heavy reliance of the local economy on mining exports. (published 0209 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA FINANCE MINISTER: 2011 ACTUAL BUDGET DEFICIT 1.27% OF GDP VS 2.1% TARGET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia recorded a 2011 budget deficit of 1.27% of gross domestic product, Finance Minister Agus Martowardojo said Thursday, well below the government's 2.1% target partly due to slow disbursement of capital expenditure. (published 0648 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : DECEMBER INFLATION LOWER THAN EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's December inflation data came in lower than what the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  had previously expected but 2011's inflation was still in line with its projection, a senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said Thursday. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINE INFLATION SLOWS, STOKES POLICY EASING VIEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines slowed in December due to stabilizing food prices, raising expectations the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will ease policy as early as January to spur growth. (published 0451 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINES RAISES $1.5 BLN VIA 2037 GLOBAL BOND PRICED AT 5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines said Thursday it raised $1.5 billion through a new 25-year global bond that was issued at a record-low yield for one of Asia's most active sovereign borrowers. (published 0332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MANILA ELECTRIC\f28 \uc2 \f2  RAISES PHP3 BLN VIA 7-, 10-YEAR NOTES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Manila Electric Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the Philippines' largest power distributor by sales, Thursday said it has raised PHP3 billion from selling seven- and 10-year fixed-rate notes to a group of institutional lenders. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LOTTE SHOPPING PLANNING OFFSHORE YUAN BOND ISSUE IN HONG KONG - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean department store operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lotte Shopping Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is planning an offshore yuan bond in Hong Kong, a person familiar with the situation said Thursday. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FAST RETAILING DEC SAME-STORE SALES UP 14.2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fast Retailing\f28 \uc2 \f2  Co. said Thursday that same-store sales at its Uniqlo casual clothing chain in Japan in December jumped 14.2% from a year earlier, thanks to strong demand for winter clothing. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEC: TO BOOK Y18.5B SECURITIES VALUATION LOSS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEC Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it would book a securities evaluation loss of Y18.5 billion at the end of the third quarter of its 2011 business year. (published 0647 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MCDONALD'S JAPAN DEC SAME-STORE SALES UP 5.0% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 McDonald's Holdings Co. Ltd. said Thursday sales at its existing stores climbed 5.0% in December from the previous year, while sales for the 2011 calendar year rose 1.0%, for the eighth consecutive year of increase. (published 0655 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA MAY LAUNCH SECURITIES FINANCING FIRM AS EARLY AS MARCH - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Securities Finance Corp., an intermediary body set up by Chinese authorities to help expand the country's nascent margin trading and short selling market, may open for business as early as March, a person familiar with the situation said Thursday. (published 0608 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SEAGATE LIFTS 2Q, 3Q REVENUE VIEWS ON HIGHER SHIPMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Seagate Technology PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  lifted its revenue outlook for its fiscal second and third quarters as the impact from Thailand flooding wasn't as bad as expected and the company benefited from higher pricing. (published 0027 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAMSUNG ELECTRONICS\f28 \uc2 \f2  EXECUTIVE: HOME APPLIANCE UNIT EYES OVER 15% SALES GROWTH IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its home appliance business targets more than 15% sales growth this year from a year earlier, largely helped by the company's increasing presence in the high-end product markets despite the ongoing global economic weakness, a company executive said. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SK GROUP: TO INVEST KRW19.1 TLN IN 2012 VS KRW9 TLN IN 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SK Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday total expenditure in 2012 will be KRW19.1 trillion, more than double the KRW9 trillion the South Korean conglomerate spent last year. (published 0546 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA'S CSR EXPECTS NET PROFIT RISE AS RAIL FIRMS GET CASH INJECTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Railway equipment maker CSR Corp. said Thursday it expects a sharp increase in net profit for 2011, the same day a major newspaper reported its unlisted parent had received a cash injection from the Chinese government. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ELPIDA: IN TALKS WITH MULTIPLE CLIENT COS ON POSSIBLE FINANCIAL SUPPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elpida Memory Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it is in talks with various client companies about the possibility of receiving financial support from them, as the Japanese maker of semiconductors tries to shore up its capital base while it struggles with weak chip prices and the yen's strength. (published 0204 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NIPPON STEEL: TO BOOK Y84.6B VALUATION LOSS FOR OCT-DEC 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nippon Steel Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that it will likely book valuation losses totaling Y84.6 billion for the October to December period due to a write-down on some of its securities holdings. (published 0247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: EX-OLYMPUS CEO WOODFORD SAYS NEAR DECISION ON PROXY FIGHT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Michael Woodford, the ousted former chief executive of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Olympus Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., said Thursday he will soon make a decision on whether to formally launch a proxy fight to unseat current management at the camera and endoscope maker, embroiled in scandal after admitting covering up $1.5 billion in investment losses dating back to the 1990s. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: TRANSPACIFIC FOUNDER SUES OVER 2011 SHARE ISSUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Transpacific Industries Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that Terry Peabody, its founder and former executive chairman, is suing the trash collection company after it barred \f28 \uc2 \f2 KKR & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . from participating in a share issue late last year. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HONG KONG REGULATOR APPROVES SIX \f28 \uc2 \f2 DEUTSCHE BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  SYNTHETIC ETFS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's securities regulator has approved six \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  synthetic exchange-traded funds, the first time it has authorized such products since July 2010. (published 0423 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TEMASEK'S SINGBRIDGE INTERNATIONAL APPOINTS CHONG PHIT LIAN CEO OF NEW UNIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singbridge International Singapore Pte. Ltd., a unit of state-investment company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Temasek Holdings Pte. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., said Thursday it appointed airline executive Chong Phit Lian to lead one of its new units. (published 0343 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GENTING MALAYSIA UNIT SIGNS INITIAL PACT WITH TO DEVELOP PROPERTY IN NEW YORK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Genting Malaysia Bhd. Thursday said its wholly-owned unit, Genting New York LLC, has signed a non-binding letter of intent with New York State Urban Development Corp for the development of an integrated mixed-use complex in New York. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY UP, BUT EUROPE CONCERNS CAP GAINS; FINANCIALS WEAK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 05-01-12 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Most Asian stock markets were modestly higher Thursday, but fresh euro-zone concerns tempered sentiment even as investors tried to build on the solid gains posted at the start of the new year. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: LYNAS SET FOR MALAYSIA DECISION ON RARE-EARTHS PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lynas Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that Malaysian authorities are nearing a decision on whether it can switch on a rare-earths processing plant in the country, potentially allowing it to start \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as early as next month. (published 0144 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINOPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  GROUP AIMS TO RAISE OVERSEAS EQUITY OIL OUTPUT TO 1 MLN BPD BY 2015 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Petrochemical Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the nation's largest oil refiner, said Thursday that it plans to more than double its equity oil output from overseas projects to more than 50 million metric tons a year, or 1 million barrels a day, by 2015 from 22.88 million tons in 2011. (published 0317 GMT)<L INK: system=djm;xrf="BJS26499">\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CISA: CHINA 2011 STEEL OUTPUT LIKELY 683 MILLION TONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's total crude steel output likely rose 9.2% in 2011 to 683 million metric tons, the China Iron and Steel Association said in a statement Thursday. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: NATURAL RUBBER OUTPUT TO BE HIT BY FLOODS IN SOUTH THAILAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ongoing heavy rain and flash floods in south Thailand will hit natural rubber production, Thai Rubber Association President Pongsak Kerdvongbundit said Thursday. (published 0654 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA DECEMBER CPO OUTPUT LIKELY FELL 10%-15% DUE TO RAIN -EXECUTIVES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude palm oil output in Malaysia probably fell 10%-15% in December because heavy rain in key growing areas hampered harvesting, industry executives said Thursday. (published 0449 GMT) [ 05-01-12 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120105e815000a9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
