\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 649 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2012\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA GOVT: KEY INDICATORS SOFTER; INFLATION UNCERTAINTIES LINGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Ministry of Strategy and Finance on Thursday repeated its warning about growing economic uncertainty, citing risks posed by the euro-zone sovereign debt crisis and political instability in the Middle East. (published 0118 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC SUSPENDS THURSDAY'S OPEN MARKET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suspended its regular open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday, thereby injecting funds into the market in Beijing's latest attempt to provide support to the country's slowing economy, people familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: HK BUSINESS ACTIVITY CONTRACTS FOR 5TH STRAIGHT MONTH IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business activity in Hong Kong contracted for the fifth straight month in December due to the slowdown in the global economy, though it sill showed improvement from the previous month as new orders increased for the first time since July, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA COMMERCE MINISTER: 2011 TRADE SURPLUS ABOUT $160 BLN - XINHUA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's trade surplus likely further narrowed last year to around $160 billion, Xinhua news agency on Thursday cited Commerce Minister Chen Deming as saying. (published 0449 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EX-PBOC ADVISER: YUAN WOULD NOT RISE SHARPLY IF PBOC HALTS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese yuan is not likely to rise significantly, and may even depreciate, if the People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stops \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market, a former \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser said Thursday. (published 0419 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S GOKARN: WILL RESPOND STRONGLY TO ANY SHARP ONE-WAY MOVES IN RUPEE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stands ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to smooth any sharp moves in the rupee, which is expected to stabilize now after falling sharply last year, a senior \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  official said Thursday. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S GOKARN: CURRENT RUPEE VALUATION MOVING TOWARD NEUTRALITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India Deputy Governor Subir Gokarn said Thursday that measures the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  took last year to stabilize the rupee's price action appear to be working and that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now appears be moving toward a more neutral valuation. (published 0424 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA TRADE SURPLUS SHOWS SIGNS OF COOLING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's trade surplus fell short of expectations during November, reflecting slower demand from Asia-based customers and underscoring the heavy reliance of the local economy on mining exports. (published 0209 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA DECEMBER CPI LIKELY UP AROUND 4% ON-YEAR; 2011 CPI LIKELY UP 5.4% -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's inflation rate may stand at around 4% in December, while the country's 2011 inflation rate is likely to be around 5.4%, the state-run China Securities Journal reported Thursday, citing analysts. (published 2344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK INDONESIA DEPUTY GOV: ABLE TO USE POLICIES TO STEM ECONOMIC DECLINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia can institute policy measures to address any decline in the domestic economy without the risk of significantly stoking inflationary pressures, according to comments on presentation slides ahead of a speech by one of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's executives Thursday. (published 0202 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINE INFLATION SLOWS, STOKES POLICY EASING VIEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines slowed in December due to stabilizing food prices, raising expectations the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will ease policy as early as January to spur growth. (published 0451 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE FINANCE CHIEF: EXPECT CREDIT RATING UPGRADE SOON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines will likely get a credit ratings upgrade soon, and, if markets are to be believed, it should be to investment grade, Finance Secretary Cesar Purisima said Thursday. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINES RAISES $1.5 BLN VIA 2037 GLOBAL BOND PRICED AT 5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines said Thursday it raised $1.5 billion through a new 25-year global bond that was issued at a record-low yield for one of Asia's most active sovereign borrowers. (published 0332 GMT) [ 