\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 811 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2012\par 06:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA GOVT: KEY INDICATORS SOFTER; INFLATION UNCERTAINTIES LINGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Ministry of Strategy and Finance on Thursday repeated its warning about growing economic uncertainty, citing risks posed by the euro-zone sovereign debt crisis and political instability in the Middle East. (published 0118 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC SUSPENDS THURSDAY'S OPEN MARKET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suspended its regular open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday, thereby injecting funds into the market in Beijing's latest attempt to provide support to the country's slowing economy, people familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: HK BUSINESS ACTIVITY CONTRACTS FOR 5TH STRAIGHT MONTH IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business activity in Hong Kong contracted for the fifth straight month in December due to the slowdown in the global economy, though it sill showed improvement from the previous month as new orders increased for the first time since July, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA COMMERCE MINISTER: 2011 TRADE SURPLUS ABOUT $160 BLN - XINHUA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's trade surplus likely further narrowed last year to around $160 billion, Xinhua news agency on Thursday cited Commerce Minister Chen Deming as saying. (published 0449 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EX-PBOC ADVISER: YUAN WOULD NOT RISE SHARPLY IF PBOC HALTS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese yuan is not likely to rise significantly, and may even depreciate, if the People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stops \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market, a former \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser said Thursday. (published 0419 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S GOKARN: CURRENT RUPEE VALUATION MOVING TOWARD NEUTRALITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India Deputy Governor Subir Gokarn said Thursday that measures the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  took last year to stabilize the rupee's price action appear to be working and that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now appears be moving toward a more neutral valuation. (published 0424 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S GOKARN: RUPEE DEPRECIATION RAISING OIL IMPORT BILL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India Deputy Governor Subir Gokarn Thursday said the rupee's depreciation is stoking inflationary pressures by raising India's oil import bill, even as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expects the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stabilize in the near term after slowing its decline over the past month. (published 0249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA TRADE SURPLUS SHOWS SIGNS OF COOLING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's trade surplus fell short of expectations during November, reflecting slower demand from Asia-based customers and underscoring the heavy reliance of the local economy on mining exports. (published 0209 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA DECEMBER CPI LIKELY UP AROUND 4% ON-YEAR; 2011 CPI LIKELY UP 5.4% -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's inflation rate may stand at around 4% in December, while the country's 2011 inflation rate is likely to be around 5.4%, the state-run China Securities Journal reported Thursday, citing analysts. (published 2344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA MAY LAUNCH SECURITIES FINANCING FIRM AS EARLY AS MARCH - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Securities Finance Corp., a centralized intermediary which is tasked to help expand domestic brokerages' margin trading and short selling businesses, may open for business as early as in March, a person familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires on Thursday. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA REGULATOR TO DELAY STRICTER CAPITAL RULES FOR BANKS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is not likely to implement stricter criteria for commercial banks' capital adequacy ratios until July given current economic conditions and looser monetary policies, the China Daily reported Thursday, citing an unnamed government source. (published 2348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: CHINA SHOULD ESTABLISH REGULATOR FOR STATE-OWNED FINANCIAL FIRMS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should establish a regulatory body to manage the government's assets in state-owned financial firms according to a clearly defined mandate, Xia Bin, an adviser to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was quoted as saying Thursday by the China Securities Journal. (published 0040 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK INDONESIA DEPUTY GOV: ABLE TO USE POLICIES TO STEM ECONOMIC DECLINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia can institute policy measures to address any decline in the domestic economy without the risk of significantly stoking inflationary pressures, according to comments on presentation slides ahead of a speech by one of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's executives Thursday. (published 0202 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINE INFLATION SLOWS, STOKES POLICY EASING VIEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines slowed in December due to stabilizing food prices, raising expectations the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will ease policy as early as January to spur growth. (published 0451 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GOVERNOR: INFLATION REMAINS MANAGEABLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines remains manageable, and adverse developments in the Middle East are the main risk to the benign outlook, Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas Governor Amando Tetangco said Thursday. (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINES RAISES $1.5 BLN VIA 2037 GLOBAL BOND PRICED AT 5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines said Thursday it raised $1.5 billion through a new 25-year global bond that was issued at a record-low yield for one of Asia's most active sovereign borrowers. (published 0332 GMT) [ 05-01-12 0500GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120105e8150006n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
