\par\par \b \uc2 Financial Services Top Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2012\par 16:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FINANCIAL SERVICES TOP STORIES \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 UNICREDIT\f28 \uc2 \f2  PRICE RIGHTS ISSUE AT BIG DISCOUNT, SHARES SINK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  offers a hefty discount on new shares it is selling to raise \u8364\'20\'AC7.5 billion it needs to meet tough new European capital requirements, signaling how expensive it could be for other lenders to follow suit in choppy markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MF GLOBAL SOLD ASSETS TO GOLDMAN BEFORE COLLAPSE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MF Global Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  sold securities worth hundreds of millions of dollars to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  on October 27, just days before it filed for bankruptcy, Reuters reports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CFTC WON'T DELAY POSITION LIMITS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Commodity Futures Trading Commission rejects a request by two trade groups to delay its implementation of position limits aimed at curtailing bets in the commodities markets, say two people familiar with the matter.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA 2012 NATIONAL FINANCING SEEN AT $2.2T \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's total national financing, a measure of growth in overall credit in the country, will likely rise to around $2.2 trillion this year from an estimated $2.06 trillion in 2011, according to a research report.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FED TO START PUBLISHING RATE FORECASTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials will begin publishing their forecasts for interest rates later this month, part of a communications revamp that could help bolster the fragile U.S. economic recovery.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HUNGARY CDS COSTS HIT FRESH RECORD HIGH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The cost of insuring Hungarian debt against default rises to a new high for the second consecutive day amid concerns the government's unorthodox policies will derail progress of a new financial agreement with the IMF.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN BOURSES SEEK ANTITRUST CLEARANCE FOR MERGER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Tokyo Stock Exchange and Osaka Securities Exchange submit a merger application to Japan's antitrust watchdog and seek a legal framework for their integration.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -TRADE CONTROVERSY SWELLS AROUND SNB PRESIDENT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A controversy surrounding transactions made by the wife of Swiss National Bank President Philipp Hildebrand swells after media reports that he profited from a large dollar purchase around the time of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  BUILDS OUT YUAN PAYMENT SYSTEM \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is building out a payment system that will make it more efficient for banks to clear yuan funds across its borders, in another move aimed at promoting the global use of the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . [ 01-04-12 1000ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120104e8140009p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
