\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2011\par 06:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN NOV INDUS OUTPUT FALLS 2.6%, BUT FORECASTS FOR COMING MOS MORE UPBEAT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese industrial production fell 2.6% in November from the previous month, but analysts were encouraged by surprisingly strong forecasts for December and January. (published 0057 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: US CRITICIZES JAPAN, CHINA ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The Obama administration again declined to label China a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manipulator, while it criticized Japan's efforts to limit the yen's appreciation. (published 0242 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FURUKAWA: TO KEEP MONITORING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MKT, TAKE APPROPRIATE STEPS IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Economy Minister Motohisa Furukawa said Wednesday the nation's policy stance toward the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market remains unchanged, even after the U.S. Treasury's criticism of Tokyo's recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0423 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VICE PREMIER LI: MAINTAIN PROACTIVE FISCAL POLICY IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Vice Premier Li Keqiang reiterated that China will maintain a proactive fiscal policy next year, the official Xinhua News Agency reported Tuesday. (published 2320 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FINANCE MINISTER: ECONOMIC CONDITIONS TO STAY TOUGH IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan reiterated Wednesday that economic conditions will remain difficult next year, asking various parts of government to ensure they are prepared to respond to rapid changes in the environment. (published 2319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA BANK ECONOMISTS: SEE 2 OR MORE RESERVE REQUIREMENT CUTS IN 1H \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is likely to cut its reserve requirement ratio for banks at least twice during the first half of 2012, but it is unlikely to adjust interest rates in the short term, economists from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA BUSINESS OUTLOOK INDEX FALLS TO 29-MONTH LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An index measuring South Korean manufacturers' outlook on business conditions in the upcoming month fell to its lowest level in almost two and a half years, lending further support to the view that the Bank of Korea isn't likely to resume raising its benchmark interest rate in the near future. (published 0214 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: KOREA REGULATOR SAYS TO ENSURE FINANCIAL MARKET STABILITY AT ALL COSTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's financial regulator said its top policy priority for 2012 is maintaining the stability of the local financial markets and it won't shy away from taking extreme measures if necessary. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: THAI NOV INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION INDEX FALLS 48.6% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's industrial production index plunged 48.6% in November compared with the same month a year earlier to 97.90, as severe flooding hurt the country's manufacturing industry, the Ministry of Industry's Office of Industrial Economics said Wednesday. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA PARLIAMENT COMMITTEE PASSES REVISED CORPORATE TAX RATE BILL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A South Korean parliament committee on Wednesday passed a revised version of a corporate income-tax plan that lowers the tax rate for companies making KRW20 billion or less. (published 0301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA FIN MINISTER: BUDGET DEFICIT 0.6% OF GDP AS OF TUESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesian government's recorded a budget deficit equivalent to 0.6% of the country's gross domestic product as of Tuesday, Finance Minister Agus Martowardojo said Wednesday. (published 0304 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM APPLIES 4% IMPORT TAX ON GASOLINE, JET FUEL EFFECTIVE TODAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam has applied an import tax of 4% on gasoline and jet fuel from Wednesday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said. (published 0416 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WESTERN AUSTRALIA 2011-12 STATE BUDGET SURPLUS ESTIMATED AT A$209M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Western Australia state government lowered its 2011-12 budget surplus forecast to A$209 million from a May forecast of A$442 million on Wednesday blaming the darkening global environment. (published 0406 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINES IMPORT GROWTH SLOWS TO 5-MONTH LOW IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The value of Philippine imports rose 2.3% from a year earlier in October, the slowest growth in five months, suggesting exports will slow as the majority of imports are used as raw materials in the manufacture of export items. (published 0456 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 28-12-11 0500GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111228e7cs0005j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
