\par\par \b \uc2 China SAFE Official: Daily Yuan Falls Do Not Equal Depreciation - Report\b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2011\par 02:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--The Chinese yuan's recent falls by its daily limit against the U.S. dollar do not equate to depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the China Business News reported Monday, citing an official with the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator.\par \par \uc2 Guan Tao, head of the State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Balance of Payments Division, noted that the yuan has recovered by the close of trading in recent sessions in which it has hit its daily downside limit, suggesting a cap to selling pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Guan also said that the benefits of changes in China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  situation--in particular the first monthly drop in China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings in eight years in October--outweighed disadvantages, and would help toward China's goal of trimming its surplus, make macroeconomic adjustments more effective and reduce trade protectionism and pressure to revalue the yuan.\par \par \uc2 "It's not true that the more \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves China seeks, the better," Guan was quoted as saying.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings fell by CNY89.34 billion ($14.07 billion) to CNY23.29 trillion ($3.67 trillion) in October.\par \par \uc2 The yuan's recent two-way fluctuation, after a period of steady appreciation, is in keeping with reforms to liberalize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate, the paper quoted Guan as saying.\par \par \uc2 The yuan hit a record high in intraday trade against the dollar Friday in what traders said were signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its daily downside limit against the dollar in 11 out of the 12 previous sessions.\par \par \uc2 Newspaper website: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.yicai.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.yicai.com/}}}\par \par \uc2 -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 8621 6120-1200; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com [ 19-12-11 0135GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111219e7cj0001y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
