\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 838 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2011\par 06:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: ECB SIGNALS INCREASED ROLE IN BATTLING DEBT IF GOVTS ENFORCE TOUGHER DEFICIT CUTTING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The messages came a day after central banks around the world acted to ease funding for banks struck by a Europe-center credit crunch, and as pressure rose on euro-zone leaders to find a breakthrough by their summit next Friday. (published 0131 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SENATE COMES UP SHORT IN ATTEMPT TO RENEW PAYROLL TAX CUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. Senate on Thursday came up short in an attempt to renew a popular payroll tax cut, and Republicans bucked their own leaders by voting against an alternative that was designed to appeal to the GOP caucus. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN MOF CAPEX SURVEY SUGGESTS 3Q GDP LIKELY LOWERED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese business investment posted its sharpest drop in almost two years during the July-September period as firms rein in spending due to the hazy global economic outlook and the strong yen. (published 0258 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN AZUMI: WON'T HESITATE TO ACT IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MKTS IF SPECULATIVE MOVES SEEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister said Friday he will not tolerate speculation-driven rises in the yen, and he reiterated his pledge to order \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if he deems it necessary. (published 0006 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S BIG FOUR BANKS ISSUED MORE THAN CNY140 BLN NEW YUAN LOANS IN NOV - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Big Four state-run banks issued more than CNY140 billion combined in new yuan loans from Nov. 1 to Nov. 28, indicating that the new yuan loans issued by the country's financial institutions in November likely totalled around CNY500 billion, sharply lower than the market expectations of CNY600 billion, the state-run China Securities Journal reported Friday, citing unnamed sources. (published 2337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EX-PBOC ADVISER: CHINA'S PROPERTY, DEBT PROBLEMS EXAGGERATED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economy remains on course and is not anywhere near to hitting the rocks, former \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser Yu Yongding wrote in a commentary published by the state-run China Daily Friday. (published 2358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S PM SAYS ON TRACK FOR 300,000 NEW JOBS IN 2 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Prime Minister Julia Gillard said Friday the economy is on track to create 300,000 more jobs in the next two years. (published 2331 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BANK OF KOREA BUYS MORE GOLD TO DIVERSIFY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN-EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea said Friday it has increased the amount of gold held as part of the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves for the second time this year, diversifying away from the U.S. dollar and toward an asset widely considered a safer bet during a crisis. (published 0140 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: US SENATE VOTES UNANIMOUSLY TO SANCTION IRAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. Senate on Thursday voted to make it harder for Iran to access the global financial system, aiming to choke off the country's ability to process oil revenue amid concerns it aims to develop a nuclear weapon. (published 0416 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2  GOV: SEE MORE ROOM FOR MONETARY POLICY FLEXIBILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  Gov. Prasarn Trairatvorakul said Friday there is more room for monetary policy flexibility after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its key policy rate for the first time since April 2009 by 25 basis points to 3.25% Wednesday. (published 0222 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2  GOV: INTEREST RATE NOT ON DOWNWARD TREND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  Gov. Prasarn Trairatvorakul said Friday its interest rate isn't on a downward trend and the bank's monetary policy easing is aimed at coping with the economic impact from the country's worst floods in decades. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : BAHT TO BE MORE VOLATILE TOWARD YEAR-END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday the baht will likely be more volatile toward the end of the year as market activity around that time is usually thin, so any small movement may cause a large swing in the Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0302 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM FINANCE MINISTRY AGENCY FORECASTS DEC CPI UP 0.5%-0.6% ON MONTH - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's consumer price index is forecast to rise 0.5%-0.6% in December from the previous month, accelerating from a 0.39% rise in November and 0.36% growth in October, state television said Friday, citing a Finance Ministry agency. (published 0221 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par      ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: TAIWAN NOV CPI LIKELY PICKED UP; EXPORTS LIKELY DOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in Taiwan likely picked up slightly in November due to higher oil and food prices, while export growth probably slowed further because of weakening demand for the island's electronic products. (published 0413 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MONEY TALKS: CRISIS-RESISTANT AUSTRALIAN DOLLAR A THREAT TO ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even with far less fiscal and monetary ammunition to steady the economy than they had during the 2008 global financial crisis, Australian policy makers believe they're well-prepared in case the euro zone's debt problems devolve into a full-blown crisis in coming months. (published 0359 GMT) [ 02-12-11 0505GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111202e7c20006o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
