\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2011\par 02:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MOF SURVEY: JUL-SEP CAPEX DOWN 9.8% ON YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business investment in Japan fell 9.8% from a year earlier in the July-September quarter, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday, showing pessimism among firms amid weakening overseas economies and the strong yen. (published 2357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN AZUMI: WON'T HESITATE TO ACT IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MKTS IF SPECULATIVE MOVES SEEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister said Friday he will not tolerate speculation-driven rises in the yen, and he reiterated his pledge to order \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if he deems it necessary. (published 0006 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S BIG FOUR BANKS ISSUED MORE THAN CNY140 BLN NEW YUAN LOANS IN NOV - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Big Four state-run banks issued more than CNY140 billion combined in new yuan loans from Nov. 1 to Nov. 28, indicating that the new yuan loans issued by the country's financial institutions in November likely totalled around CNY500 billion, sharply lower than the market expectations of CNY600 billion, the state-run China Securities Journal reported Friday, citing unnamed sources. (published 2337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EX-PBOC ADVISER: CHINA'S PROPERTY, DEBT PROBLEMS EXAGGERATED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economy remains on course and is not anywhere near to hitting the rocks, former \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser Yu Yongding wrote in a commentary published by the state-run China Daily Friday. (published 2358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S PM SAYS ON TRACK FOR 300,000 NEW JOBS IN 2 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Prime Minister Julia Gillard said Friday the economy is on track to create 300,000 more jobs in the next two years. (published 2331 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF KOREA BUYS GOLD FOR SECOND TIME THIS YEAR TO DIVERSIFY PORTFOLIO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea said Friday it has increased the amount of gold held as part of the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves for the second time this year, diversifying away from the U.S. dollar and toward an asset widely considered a safer bet during a crisis. (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 02-12-11 0100GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111202e7c200019\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
