\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Stocks Surge On Central Banks, China, Jobs\b0\par\par\uc2 1,252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2011\par 22:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 4:16 (Dow Jones) US stocks climb more than 4% buoyed by coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's cut to its bank-reserve requirements and a better-than-expected rise in ADP's private payrolls report. DJIA gains 490, or 4.2%, to 12045.68, its biggest rise since March 2009. S&P 500 ends up 52 at 1246.96 and the Nasdaq Comp climbs 104 to 2620.34. Still many analysts downplay today's moves as a true turning point and the move in Treasurys is not as pronounced with the 10-year yields up to 2.075%. (patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 4:06 (Dow Jones) Though Weatherford (WFT) was built into a global oilfield service giant largely with acquisitions, takeovers are playing a "smaller and smaller and smaller role" in the company's growth, CEO Bernard Duroc-Danner tells Dahlman Rose conference. "We essentially have what we need to build what we're trying to build," Duroc-Danner says. Rather than buy, WFT is now a seller, eyeing to shed some $1 billion worth of non-core businesses one-by-one -- "nothing terribly important, no big numbers," he says -- over the next couple of years. WFT rides broader rally, up 7.01% to $15.11.(ryan.dezember@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 4:01 (Dow Jones) Lending in the health care sector continues to be a bright spot for \uc2 Fifth Third Bancorp\uc2  (FITB). Now, health care even has a spot on the board. The Cincinnati bank said Wednesday it appointed \uc2 Humana Inc\uc2 . (HUM) Chairman and CEO \uc2 Michael McCallister\uc2  as director. President Obama's health care changes are only one reason why the health care sector is borrowing, and that is good for banks that are struggling to find enough qualified borrowers. "We are eager to have his insights and expertise," said CEO \uc2 Kevin Kabat\uc2 . (matthias.rieker@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:53 (Dow Jones) Shares of \uc2 Zoltek\uc2  (ZOLT) climb 41% to $8.09 after company posts better-than-expected fiscal 4Q earnings late Tuesday helped by a gain in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions. DA Davidson expects growth in company's wind power business to drive revenue as it upgrades shares to buy from neutral. Dougherty & Co. raises its price target to $10 from $9 for the maker of carbon and technical fibers.(patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:42 (Dow Jones) Treasury prices fell, but not as much as the surge in US equities would suggest. Ten-year yields are up just eight basis points to 2.075%, while 30-year bond yields are up 11 bps to 3.065%. "Bond investors are looking at the German auction and high yields offered at the Italian auction, and saying the [joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] action today doesn't address those issues," said Kevin Flanagan, interest-rate strategist at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 . The firm sees 10-year yields ending the year at 2% and ticking up to 2.25% at the end of 2012. (cynthia.lin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:39 (Dow Jones) Oil-and-gas companies using fracking to drill in shale plays should be taking seriously the possible risk of the drilling technique causing earthquakes, says \uc2 MicroSeismic\uc2  Chairman \uc2 Peter Duncan\uc2  at Jefferies' energy conference. He contends there's rising evidence that the increase used of fracking is related with the elevated occurrence of seismic activity in areas such as Ohio and in the UK. But others have discounted that sentiment. (Isabel.ordonez@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:33 (Dow Jones) Though the projected 3.1% growth in November same-store sales, compiled from a survey of analysts by Thomson Reuters, may not look that hot considering gains in recent months, keep in mind that last November saw a 5.5% jump. Meanwhile, the data--largely being released Thursday morning--will give company-specific reads on how activity this past weekend was. And it's key for November SSS. \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  notes many retailers generate about 25% of the month's sales on Black Friday and the day after. They happen to be the final two days of the November sales period. (karen.talley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:26 (Dow Jones) AMR couldn't get through Wednesday without trading pause, as shares pare gains sharply in afternoon trading. Traders suffered through 16 pauses Tuesday. \uc2 NYSE Euronext\uc2  (NYX) said Tuesday had AMR under review and could suspend trading at any time; spokesman as of mid-Wednesday said no new announcement on AMR's status. Tough road for AMR to surmount $1, level NYSE rules require stocks to keep average price for 30 days or else lose listing. 30-day period also means AMR could hang out for while if NYSE so chooses. AMR up 7c to 33c after gaining as much as 65% in early trading. (brendan.conway@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:25 (Dow Jones) \uc2 UBS\uc2  feels Aimco (AIV) has fallen enough as it upgrades the apartment operator to neutral while trimming its price target another $2 to $21. "We downgraded AIV on Oct. 31 given weaker-than-expected traffic, occupancy and slowing rent growth. While shares may continue to underperform the REIT sector as operating trends lag, we believe the recent drop in the stock has priced in these concerns." It adds, "The recent pullback has removed the froth that we saw in the stocks, but we see the group remaining range-bound until visibility improves surrounding whether rent growth holds at current levels, or retreats modestly in 2012." AIV gains 7.2% today at $21.75 after having fallen 20% since late October. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:20 (Dow Jones) Sterne Agee likes the deal for \uc2 MasterCard\uc2  (MA) and \uc2 Western Union\uc2  (WU) to jointly develop money-transfer services. The effort, which will allow MA cardholders to send money directly from existing accounts to others using WU's network, shows the value of the latter's "underbanked client base." and helps MA in its quest to build up its prepaid-card business, a growing area for payments companies. (andrew.r.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:19 (Dow Jones) The Federal Reserve stepped up again to save the world -- or so it looks. Boosting liquidity and market confidence by lowering the pricing on its swap program with foreign central banks has long proved to help banks here and overseas overcome liquidity crunches. But it's treating a symptom, not a cause. As long as sovereign bond prices are falling, the market will struggle to find a firm footing. That's a matter of government, rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , action. "No amount of capital will help if sovereign debt keeps falling in price," says Ajay Rajadhyaksha of \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . (matthias.rieker@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:13 (Dow Jones) Orange juice futures slip in New York, with the front-month January contract settling 0.2% lower at $1.7610 a pound. "There's not much news right now," said Boyd Cruel, of Vision Financial Markets, noting that traders for the next couple of months will be scanning long-term weather forecasts for signs of possible frost in Florida. "If weather looks mild and temperatures are going to remain above freezing, that will put a lid on the market," Cruel adds. (paul.kiernan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Equities Market Talk Editors, \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Paul Vigna, 212 416-2184,paul.vigna@dowjones.com \par Visit the Market Talk website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 11-30-11 1616ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020111130e7bu001cs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
