\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -\uc2 Dexia\uc2 ,  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  PMI hit Asian  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ;  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen\b0\par\par\uc2 1,107 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2011\par 05:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Sing dlr at 7-week low, won at 1-mth low\par \par \uc2 * India, Indonesia, Singapore c.banks sell dlrs - dealers\par \par \uc2 * Baht down as offshore players sell; wary of BOT\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Nov 23 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on Wednesday with the Singapore dollar hitting a seven-week low on increasing worries about the euro zone and the global economy, though some regional units were pulled higher by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The central banks of India, Indonesia and Singapore were spotted selling dollars to bolster their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The rupee, which hit an all-time low on Tuesday, strengthened for the day, bucking the trend of peers.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players were cautious as they weighed the possibility that more central banks will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With the wariness, some investors were reluctant to sell emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively, regarding them as a bit oversold, while short-term investors such as interbank speculators unloaded regional units.\par \par \uc2 "Fear factor is up, but there is no real conviction right now. I'd rather try to catch falling knives," said a European bank dealer in Singapore, adding he would buy the Singapore dollar around 1.3070 per the U.S. dollar, around the session's low.\par \par \uc2 Another dealer in Kuala Lumpur said he would wait for "better levels" to buy the U.S. dollar against the emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , adding the market appeared to hold dollar-long positions.\par \par \uc2 The dealer said he won't buy dollars now while Asian central banks and exporters are selling them, but later he will accumulate the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because there's "too much trouble in the world."\par \par \uc2 Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have slid this month on deepening worries about European debt crisis and signs of rising dollar funding costs.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under more pressure after a Belgian newspaper reported that the Franco-Belgium bailout of \uc2 Dexia\uc2  bank -- the first casualty of the euro zone sovereign debt crisis -- was going to be the subject of new talks.\par \par \uc2 A preliminary survey on Chinese manufacturing renewed worries of a hard landing for the world's second-largest economy, boosting global recession fears, pushing down emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  further.\par \par \uc2 The media report and the \uc2 HSBC\uc2  flash purchasing managers' index (PMI) dragged down Asian stocks and the euro.\par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  "should fall further because a Chinese slowdown would hurt growth and exports for the rest of Asia," said Dariusz Kowalczyk, senior economist and strategist for Asia ex-Japan at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  CIB in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 Dollar/won hit a one-month high of 1,152.2 as foreign investors continued to sell Seoul shares. The pair breached the 50 percent Fibonacci retracement of its October slides.\par \par \uc2 It is seen facing a resistance at its previous high of 1,153.2 as investors are wary of possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities above 1,150.\par \par \uc2 "Given \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  possibilities, exporters will get more active above 1,150," said a senior foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 But some expect further gains for the dollar, considering foreign investors' massive stock sales. Foreign investors have unloaded a combined net 1.77 trillion won ($1.54 billion) during the five consecutive sessions.\par \par \uc2 RUPEE\par \par \uc2 Dollar/rupee fell as much as 1.7 percent from the session's high after state-run banks dumped dollars, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 But global risk aversion meant the dollar/rupee will remain strong in the near term.\par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have been pulling out of the shaky stock market over the past week while oil refiners who import about three-quarters of India's crude consumption have been heavy buyers of dollars in recent sessions.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar rose to 1.3074, the highest since Oct 6, but agent banks of the city-state's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were spotted selling the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders reckon the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) is keen to cap rallies in the pair to below the 1.3100 level for the time being.\par \par \uc2 However, risk aversion remains supportive of the pair with markets still keen to buy U.S. dollars on dips, targeting 1.3200, the high on Oct. 3-4.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 Dollar/rupiah rose on strong demand from foreign names while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted selling dollars, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 Dollar/baht gained as offshore players bought the pair following a weaker Singapore dollar, and the pair is seen rising more.\par \par \uc2 It may look better to buy the pair for possible breaching of 31.32 and moving to 32.00-32.10, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 But some players are wary of possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Dollar/baht will be capped around 31.30 as Asian central banks including BOT will be in the market to calm it down," said a Bangkok-based dealer.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0735 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        76.96          76.98       +0.02\par  Sing dlr        1.3050         1.3025       -0.19\par  Taiwan dlr      30.381         30.309       -0.24\par  Korean won     1150.15        1145.30       -0.42\par  Baht             31.24          31.16       -0.26\par  Peso             43.44          43.24       -0.45\par  Rupiah         9050.00        9040.00       -0.11\par  Rupee            52.12          52.27       +0.29\par  Ringgit         3.1780         3.1780       +0.00\par  Yuan            6.3551         6.3608       +0.09\par  Change so far in 2011\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        76.96          81.15       +5.44\par  Sing dlr        1.3050         1.2820       -1.76\par  Taiwan dlr      30.381         30.368       -0.04\par  Korean won     1150.15        1134.80       -1.33\par  Baht             31.24          30.14       -3.52\par  Peso             43.44          43.84       +0.93\par  Rupiah         9050.00        9005.00       -0.50\par  Rupee            52.12          44.70      -14.24\par  Ringgit         3.1780         3.0820       -3.02\par  Yuan            6.3551         6.5897       +3.69\par \f28 \par \par \uc