\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For November 18\b0\par\par\uc2 1,414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2011\par 08:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA PROPERTY PRICES POST FIRST DECLINE SINCE GOVERNMENT CURBS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Average property prices in 70 Chinese cities covered in a government survey fell slightly in October from a month ago, recording their first on-month decline since Beijing started a two-year tightening campaign to cool the red-hot property market and suggesting the start of a much anticipated correction in prices. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA REAL HOUSEHOLD INCOME +1.6% ON YR IN 3Q VS +0.5% IN 2Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's real average household income rose at a faster pace in the third quarter compared with the second quarter on improved employment conditions, data from Statistics Korea showed Friday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US LOCKE: CHINESE YUAN SHOULD FLOAT FREELY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should float freely, Gary Locke, U.S. ambassador to China, said Friday. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC ADVISER: CHINA SHOULD JOIN WITH IMF TO AID EUROPE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should join forces with the International Monetary Fund and countries such as Russia to aid Europe, Li Daokui, an academic adviser to the People's Bank of China, said Friday. (published 0452 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA PREMIER WEN: GLOBAL ECONOMIC UNCERTAINTIES, INSTABILITY MAY EXIST IN LONG TERM - XINHUA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Premier Wen Jiabao said at a summit between China and the Association of Southeast Asian Nations Thursday that global economic uncertainties and instabilities may remain in the long term, adding that the two sides should move forward toward existing targets, the official Xinhua News Agency reported Friday. (published 0527 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: SHOULD USE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN YUAN RATE - REPORT \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should use its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to adjust the yuan's exchange rate, People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin was quoted as saying by the state-run Economic Information Daily Friday. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EX-PBOC ADVISER: CHINA 2012 GDP GROWTH LIKELY TO EASE TO 8.6%-8.7% - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic growth will likely ease to 8.6%-8.7% in 2012 and inflation will be controllable next year, the China Business News reported Friday, citing Fan Gang, a former adviser to China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0124 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE MAS: RISKS TO FINANCIAL STABILITY INCREASED SIGNIFICANTLY IN 2H \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Risks to global financial stability have increased significantly in the second half of this year and a protracted global slowdown could weigh on Singapore's economy--considered a bellwether for the region--the island nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a report. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC BRANCH TO ADJUST BANK RESERVE CALCULATION TO SPUR LENDING TO SMALL FIRMS - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's branch in the coastal city of Tianjin plans to include loans to smaller businesses in the calculation of banks' reserve requirements, in a move aimed at encouraging lenders to offer more support for enterprises suffering from a credit squeeze under Beijing's tight monetary controls, people familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires Friday. (published 0608 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES BALANCE OF PAYMENTS SURPLUS NARROWS TO $208 MLN IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines registered a balance of payments surplus of $208 million in October, much narrower than a surplus of $2.74 billion a year earlier, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0447 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OKS REVISIONS TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RULES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday said it approved additional changes to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rules to make them "attuned to current economic conditions" and ease \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions with banks. (published 0524 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: TAIWAN OCT EXPORT ORDERS, INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT LIKELY PICKED UP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in Taiwan's export orders and industrial output likely picked up in October, driven by year-end holiday sales, but economists remain cautious about global demand through the next quarter as the euro-zone debt problem wears on. (published 0233 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAB MILLER TO PAY EXTRA A$582M FOR FOSTER'S AFTER TAX RULING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SABMiller PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  will have to pay an extra A$582 million as part of its takeover of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Foster's Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., after the Australian Taxation Office knocked back the planned structure of the deal. (published 0659 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASIAN CORPORATE GOVERNANCE ASSOCIATION: URGED TOKYO BOURSE TO KEEP OLYMPUS LISTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Asian Corporate Governance Association said Friday that it has sent a letter to the Tokyo Stock Exchange urging the bourse to keep the shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Olympus Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . listed. (published 0418 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MUFG LOWERS STAKE IN OLYMPUS TO 7.6% FROM 10% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . cut its stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Olympus Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to 7.6% from 10% according to a regulatory filing, becoming the latest shareholder to reduce its exposure to the company, which is engulfed in a financial scandal. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: TELSTRA ON TRACK, REVEALS DIGITAL UNIT PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's largest telecommunications company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telstra Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that it's on track to achieve its previously stated revenue guidance and plans to create a new division to manage its digital media interests. (published 2238 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: \f28 \uc2 \f2 SAMSUNG ENGINEERING\f28 \uc2 \f2  TARGETS 22% SALES GROWTH IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Engineering Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., South Korea's No. 1 engineering firm by sales, targets sales growth of more than 20% next year, helped by demand for new plants and reconstruction efforts in war-torn countries, a senior executive at the company said. (published 0135 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par COACH WINS REGULATORY OK FOR DEPOSITORY RECEIPTS ISSUANCE IN HK; TO LIST DEC. 1 - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Coach Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to list in Hong Kong on Dec. 1 after it was approved by the Hong Kong stock exchange's listing committee Thursday to issue Hong Kong depositary receipts, a person familiar with the situation said Friday, as the U.S. handbag maker looks to raise its profile among China's rich. (published 0109 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: CHORUS CEO: TELECOM LOSING US-BASED INVESTORS AHEAD OF CHORUS SPINOFF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S.-based shareholders have been selling down their stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telecom Corp. of New Zealand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . ahead of the spinoff and separate listing of its infrastructure unit, Chorus Ltd., next week, Chorus Chief Executive Mark Ratcliffe said Friday. (published 0214 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NWS HOLDINGS\f28 \uc2 \f2 : PLAN TO RAISE STAKE IN HANGZHOU HIGHWAY PROJECT TO 95% FROM 61.75% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Infrastructure and services firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 NWS Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it plans to boost its total stake in a Hangzhou expressway project to 95% from 61.75% in a deal valued at around US$402 million, underscoring the company's optimism about demand for Chinese infrastructure assets. (published 0234 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BUKIT ASAM RAILWAYS TO GET $1.3 BLN 15-YEAR LOAN FROM CHINA DEVELOPMENT BANK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Bukit Asam Transpacific Railways, or BATR, Friday signed a preliminary agreement with China Development Bank for $1.3 billion in 15-year loan. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WYNN MACAU: TO PAY SPECIAL DIVIDEND OF HK$1.20 PER SHARE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wynn Macau Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it would pay a special dividend of HK$1.20 per share, marking the second time the Hong Kong-listed casino operator has declared such a payout. (published 0015 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPLASH PLANS PHP1.12 BLN BORROWING TO REFINANCE DEBT, FUND ACQUISITIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Splash Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a Philippine-based manufacturer of personal care products, said Friday it plans to borrow a total PHP1.12 billion to refinance debt and fund acquisitions. (published 0412 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PHILIPPINE NATIONAL BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  RAISES PHP3.1 BLN FROM DEPOSIT CERTIFICATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine National Bank said Friday it raised PHP3.1 billion from an issuance of long-term negotiable certificates of deposit. (published 0426 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE:ASIAN SHARES DROP; EUROPEAN GLOOM DEPRESSES EXPORTERS, COPPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets dropped Friday as gloom over the European sovereign-debt crisis hurt material plays and exporters particularly hard, and drove copper and most regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA IMPORTED AROUND 1 MLN TONS COTTON RECENTLY -INDUSTRY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China imported around 1 million metric tons of cotton recently for state reserves, taking advantage of low global prices, an industry website said Friday, quoting unidentified people. (published 0344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHANGHAI GOLD EXCHANGE: TO RAISE SILVER MARGINS TO 18% IF TRADING HITS DAILY LIMITS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Shanghai Gold Exchange said Friday that it will raise the trading margins of its silver forward contracts to 18% from 15% at settlement close if trading hits daily limits. (published 0335 GMT) [ 18-11-11 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111118e7bi000cw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
