\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 859 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2011\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA PROPERTY PRICES POST FIRST DECLINE SINCE GOVERNMENT CURBS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Average property prices in 70 Chinese cities covered in a government survey fell slightly in October from a month ago, recording their first on-month decline since Beijing started a two-year tightening campaign to cool the red-hot property market and suggesting the start of a much anticipated correction in prices. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA REAL HOUSEHOLD INCOME +1.6% ON YR IN 3Q VS +0.5% IN 2Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's real average household income rose at a faster pace in the third quarter compared with the second quarter on improved employment conditions, data from Statistics Korea showed Friday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC ADVISER: CHINA SHOULD JOIN WITH IMF TO AID EUROPE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should join forces with the International Monetary Fund and countries such as Russia to aid Europe, Li Daokui, an academic adviser to the People's Bank of China, said Friday. (published 0452 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF CANADA'S BOIVIN: FAILURE TO CONTAIN EURO-ZONE CRISIS A KEY DOWNSIDE RISK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada deputy governor Jean Boivin said Thursday that failure to contain the euro-zone debt crisis is a key downside risk for Canada's inflation outlook, repeating an assessment the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  made last month. (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN AZUMI: WANTS GERMANY TO WORK HARD VS EUROPE CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister on Friday voiced concerns over the intensifying debt crisis in Europe and urged Germany to play a leading role in creating a regional firewall against the turmoil to reassure the jittery financial market. (published 0045 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOE WEALE: 'VERY STRONG CASE' FOR EXTENDING QE NEXT YEAR UNLESS OUTLOOK IMPROVES - FT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Martin Weale, an external member of the Bank of England's monetary policy committee, said there is a "very strong case" for extending the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's quantitative easing policy next year unless the outlook improves, the Financial Times reported on its website. (published 0302 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECONOMISTS, MONEY MARKETS BEGINNING TO PRICE IN POSSIBLE DECEMBER RBNZ RATE CUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists and money markets are beginning to entertain the possibility of a rate cut in New Zealand in December as financial turbulence out of crisis-stricken Europe continues. (published 0309 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PREMIER WEN: GLOBAL ECONOMIC UNCERTAINTIES, INSTABILITY MAY EXIST IN LONG TERM - XINHUA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Premier Wen Jiabao said at a summit between China and the Association of Southeast Asian Nations Thursday that global economic uncertainties and instabilities may remain in the long term, adding that the two sides should move forward toward existing targets, the official Xinhua News Agency reported Friday. (published 0527 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: SHOULD USE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN YUAN RATE - REPORT \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should use its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to adjust the yuan's exchange rate, People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin was quoted as saying by the state-run Economic Information Daily Friday. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EX-PBOC ADVISER: CHINA 2012 GDP GROWTH LIKELY TO EASE TO 8.6%-8.7% - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic growth will likely ease to 8.6%-8.7% in 2012 and inflation will be controllable next year, the China Business News reported Friday, citing Fan Gang, a former adviser to China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0124 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE MAS: RISKS TO FINANCIAL STABILITY INCREASED SIGNIFICANTLY IN 2H \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Risks to global financial stability have increased significantly in the second half of this year and a protracted global slowdown could weigh on Singapore's economy--considered a bellwether for the region--the island nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a report. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES BALANCE OF PAYMENTS SURPLUS NARROWS TO $208 MLN IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines registered a balance of payments surplus of $208 million in October, much narrower than a surplus of $2.74 billion a year earlier, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0447 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OKS REVISIONS TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RULES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday said it approved additional changes to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rules to make them "attuned to current economic conditions" and ease \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions with banks. (published 0524 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: GUANGDONG PROVINCE SELLS BONDS AT LOWER-THAN-EXPECTED YIELDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Guangdong province sold China's second regional government bonds directly backed by local authorities at lower-than-expected yields Friday, the second time in a week that investors have welcomed the new fixed-income products. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: TAIWAN OCT EXPORT ORDERS, INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT LIKELY PICKED UP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in Taiwan's export orders and industrial output likely picked up in October, driven by year-end holiday sales, but economists remain cautious about global demand through the next quarter as the euro-zone debt problem wears on. (published 0233 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: CRISIS ENSNARES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN DESPERATE BID TO SAVE EURO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At a mid-July meeting of the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's governing board, the bank's longtime president, Jean-Claude Trichet, was summoned from a conference room to take an urgent call from Berlin. (published 0400 GMT) [ 18-11-11 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111118e7bi000a0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
