on Friday voiced concerns over the intensifying debt crisis in Europe and urged Germany to play a leading role in creating a regional firewall against the turmoil to reassure the jittery financial market. (published 0045 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOE WEALE: 'VERY STRONG CASE' FOR EXTENDING QE NEXT YEAR UNLESS OUTLOOK IMPROVES - FT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Martin Weale, an external member of the Bank of England's monetary policy committee, said there is a "very strong case" for extending the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's quantitative easing policy next year unless the outlook improves, the Financial Times reported on its website. (published 0302 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECONOMISTS, MONEY MARKETS BEGINNING TO PRICE IN POSSIBLE DECEMBER RBNZ RATE CUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists and money markets are beginning to entertain the possibility of a rate cut in New Zealand in December as financial turbulence out of crisis-stricken Europe continues. (published 0309 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: SHOULD USE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN YUAN RATE - REPORT \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should use its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to adjust the yuan's exchange rate, People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin was quoted as saying by the state-run Economic Information Daily Friday. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EX-PBOC ADVISER: CHINA 2012 GDP GROWTH LIKELY TO EASE TO 8.6%-8.7% - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic growth will likely ease to 8.6%-8.7% in 2012 and inflation will be controllable next year, the China Business News reported Friday, citing Fan Gang, a former adviser to China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0124 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE MAS: RISKS TO FINANCIAL STABILITY INCREASED SIGNIFICANTLY IN 2H \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Risks to global financial stability have increased significantly in the second half of this year and a protracted global slowdown could weigh on Singapore's economy--considered a bellwether for the region--the island nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a report. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES BALANCE OF PAYMENTS SURPLUS NARROWS TO $208 MLN IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines registered a balance of payments surplus of $208 million in October, much narrower than a surplus of $2.74 billion a year earlier, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0447 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC TIANJIN BRANCH PLANS TO INCLUDE LENDING TO SMALLER FIRMS IN BANK RESERVE RATIO CALCULATION -SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's branch in the coastal city of Tianjin plans to include loans to smaller businesses in the calculation of banks' reserve requirements, a move aimed at encouraging lenders to offer more support for enterprises suffering from a credit squeeze under Beijing's tight monetary controls, people familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires Friday. (published 0432 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: GUANGDONG PROVINCE SELLS BONDS AT LOWER-THAN-EXPECTED YIELDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Guangdong province sold China's second regional government bonds directly backed by local authorities at lower-than-expected yields Friday, the second time in a week that investors have welcomed the new fixed-income products. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: TAIWAN OCT EXPORT ORDERS, INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT LIKELY PICKED UP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in Taiwan's export orders and industrial output likely picked up in October, driven by year-end holiday sales, but economists remain cautious about global demand through the next quarter as the euro-zone debt problem wears on. (published 0233 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: CRISIS ENSNARES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN DESPERATE BID TO SAVE EURO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At a mid-July meeting of the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's governing board, the bank's longtime president, Jean-Claude Trichet, was summoned from a conference room to take an urgent call from Berlin. (published 0400 GMT) [ 18-11-11 0500GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111118e7bi0008f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
