NESE YUAN SHOULD FLOAT FREELY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should float freely, Gary Locke, U.S. ambassador to China, said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: CHINA SHOULD JOIN WITH IMF TO AID EUROPE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should join forces with the International Monetary Fund and countries such as Russia to aid Europe, Li Daokui, an academic adviser to the People's Bank of China, said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOE WEALE: 'VERY STRONG CASE' FOR EXTENDING QE NEXT YEAR UNLESS OUTLOOK IMPROVES - FT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Martin Weale, an external member of the Bank of England's monetary policy committee, said there is a "very strong case" for extending the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's quantitative easing policy next year unless the outlook improves, the Financial Times reported on its website.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PREMIER WEN: GLOBAL ECONOMIC UNCERTAINTIES, INSTABILITY MAY EXIST IN LONG TERM - XINHUA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Premier Wen Jiabao said at a summit between China and the Association of Southeast Asian Nations Thursday that global economic uncertainties and instabilities may remain in the long term, adding that the two sides should move forward toward existing targets, the official Xinhua News Agency reported Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: SHOULD USE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN YUAN RATE - REPORT \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should use its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to adjust the yuan's exchange rate, People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin was quoted as saying by the state-run Economic Information Daily Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EX-PBOC ADVISER: CHINA 2012 GDP GROWTH LIKELY TO EASE TO 8.6%-8.7% - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic growth will likely ease to 8.6%-8.7% in 2012 and inflation will be controllable next year, the China Business News reported Friday, citing Fan Gang, a former adviser to China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE MAS: RISKS TO FINANCIAL STABILITY INCREASED SIGNIFICANTLY IN 2H \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Risks to global financial stability have increased significantly in the second half of this year and a protracted global slowdown could weigh on Singapore's economy--considered a bellwether for the region--the island nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a report.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC BRANCH TO ADJUST BANK RESERVE CALCULATION TO SPUR LENDING TO SMALL FIRMS - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's branch in the coastal city of Tianjin plans to include loans to smaller businesses in the calculation of banks' reserve requirements, in a move aimed at encouraging lenders to offer more support for enterprises suffering from a credit squeeze under Beijing's tight monetary controls, people familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES BALANCE OF PAYMENTS SURPLUS NARROWS TO $208 MLN IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines registered a balance of payments surplus of $208 million in October, much narrower than a surplus of $2.74 billion a year earlier, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OKS REVISIONS TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RULES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday said it approved additional changes to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rules to make them "attuned to current economic conditions" and ease \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions with banks. [ 18-11-11 1100GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020111118e7bi0000u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
